te early\n  only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score.\n\n## Hard rules (violations = disqualification)\n\n1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at\n   `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat\n   everything after **2026-08-29** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards,\n   dashboard) for times after 2026-08-29 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and\n   disqualifies you. Audited on your transcript.\n2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges,\n   aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS/rank evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester`\n   (via `agent/predict.py`). This is what makes your work comparable to others'.\n4. Forbidden: falsifying the journal/results; fetching or dissecting predictions served by\n   individual miners.\n5. **ABSOLUTE prohibition on reading the operator's own private research code** (any\n   already-developed miner model outside your workspace). It should not exist anywhere in your\n   environment. If you come across it by any means whatsoever — a mount, a copy, an archive, a\n   search result — do not access it, do not read it, do not draw on it, and report it in\n   `suggestions.md`. Your work must start from public sources (synth-lib, synth-subnet, the\n   Synth API) and your own ideas.\n6. Your final champion must expose, in `agent/modeling.py`:\n   `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)`\n   -> tuple `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)` — each path: a list of\n   `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context.\n   **The `context_prices` contract, exactly**: a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days\n   preceding `start_time`, with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close`\n   is the series you are scored against; the rest are context. It MAY CONTAIN NaN in every\n   column — your `simulate()` must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate). Evaluation passes\n   the raw frame: handle gaps inside your model, not in a loader you hope evaluation shares.\n   Runnable OFFLINE (weights/artifacts committed or included in the workspace).\n\n## Required deliverables (in `agent/`)\n\nWrite `journal.md`, `report.md`, and `suggestions.md` in English — these reports are published\nto the Synth miner community.\n\n- `journal.md`: one entry per iteration — Hypothesis / Change / Result (numbers) / Verdict\n  (keep-discard) / Lesson. As you go: this is your memory if you crash.\n- `report.md`: your final report, explainer style (audience = Synth miners). Sections: context,\n  approach, experiments (failures included), results, limitations, what you'd do with more\n  budget.\n- `CHAMPION`: YAML — `sha` (an EXISTING git commit in your workspace, not a placeholder),\n  `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles`, `notes`. `profiles` must list the formats your champion\n  supports: `[low, high]` if you cover both 24h AND 1h (expected), `[low]` if you could only\n  handle the 24h. `notes` MUST include your champion's backtested rank per competition,\n  produced by the official backtester (`agent/predict.py`) at 1000 paths — a nomination\n  without field-relative numbers is incomplete. The harness checks the interface as soon as\n  this file appears (result in BUDGET.md) — fix it if the check fails.\n- `suggestions.md`: anything that falls outside your scope.\n- you must commit all deliverables to your workspace git repo before the deadline.\n# DATA.md — the shape of your market data (generated from THIS snapshot at setup)\n\nEach day is one parquet file, `date=YYYY-MM-DD.parquet`, a full 1440-row minute grid\nwith columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close` is the scored series.\nOnly `close` carries real data: the venue's 1-minute candle close (the last trade of\nthat minute). `open/high/low/volume` columns may exist but are NA in this snapshot.\n`source`/`ingested_at`/`is_final` are ingestion provenance — ignore them. Semantics:\n\n- **NaN close** = no trade that minute (thin market or feed gap). NOT market hours:\n  these venues trade 24/7. Real density varies by asset and era — see the table.\n- **Missing file** = before that market's first trade. Nothing existed; nothing is hidden.\n- Scoring drops NaN per prompt. Never interpolate: inventing prices in the gaps is how\n  you fool your own validation.\n\nPer-asset coverage, measured from this snapshot (nan% = share of NaN minutes among the\nasset's real days; first/last 30d columns show density drift — early months of newer\nlistings are genuinely thin, low realized volatility there is real):\n\n| asset | first day | last day | real days | nan% total | nan% first 30d | nan% last 30d |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AAPLX | 2025-11-21 | 2026-08-29 | 282 | 43.6% | 60.1% | 15.7% |\n| BTC | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| ETH | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| GOOGLX | 2025-11-18 | 2026-08-29 | 285 | 25.8% | 23.9% | 9.9% |\n| HYPE | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.1% | 0.1% | 0.0% |\n| NVDAX | 2025-11-12 | 2026-08-29 | 291 | 11.0% | 14.9% | 4.0% |\n| SOL | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| SP500 | 2026-03-18 | 2026-08-29 | 165 | 1.0% | 2.8% | 0.2% |\n| SPCX | 2026-05-17 | 2026-08-29 | 105 | 1.9% | 4.6% | 1.2% |\n| TSLAX | 2025-11-13 | 2026-08-29 | 290 | 14.9% | 26.2% | 12.4% |\n| WTIOIL | 2026-01-06 | 2026-08-29 | 236 | 13.2% | 58.8% | 1.9% |\n| XAU | 2025-12-22 | 2026-08-29 | 251 | 11.2% | 39.2% | 1.5% |\n| XRP | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n[project]\nname = \"campaign-workspace\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.12,<3.14\"\ndependencies = [\"synth-lib\", \"numpy>=2.2\", \"pandas>=2.3\", \"torch>=2.0\"]\n\n[tool.uv.sources]\nsynth-lib = { git = \"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib\", rev = \"782a44fe7585a4e7b0388e22b99c57f13d56f5ee\" }\n\"\"\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.\n\nThis is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.\nContract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has\ntime_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef simulate(\n    asset: str,\n    start_time,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n    context_prices=None,\n):\n    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1\n    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].dropna()\n    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\n    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\n    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0\n    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])\n\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n\nUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\nGenerates predictions from agent/modeling.py over a grid of past prompts (covered by the\nsnapshot), writes them in the standard format, then scores them with backtest() (validator\nCRPS + rank vs the real field via the Synth API).\n\n--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\ngeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\nfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import OHLCV_COLUMNS, STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.market_data import MinutePriceStore\n\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n\nfrom modeling import simulate  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n\nCONTEXT_MINUTES = 7 * 24 * 60\nPREDICTIONS_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\" / \"predictions\"\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n\n    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n\n\ndef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n\n    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n\n\ndef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n\n    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(asset)\n    missing = []\n    cursor = start.date()\n    while cursor <= end.date():\n        if not (root / f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\").exists():\n            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only) and stops at the campaign's data_cutoff. \"\n            f\"Reduce --eval-end / --days to stay within the available coverage ({root}).\"\n        )\n\n\ndef generate(\n    asset: str,\n    start: datetime,\n    end: datetime,\n    cadence_minutes: int = 60,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n) -> int:\n    store = MinutePriceStore(asset, root=store_root(asset))\n    df = store.load_range(start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end).set_index(\"timestamp\")\n    prices = df[OHLCV_COLUMNS]\n    PREDICTIONS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    end_ts = pd.Timestamp(end)\n    n = 0\n    for t in pd.date_range(start, end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\"):\n        if t >= end_ts:\n            break\n        context = prices.loc[:t][-CONTEXT_MINUTES:]\n        out = simulate(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n        payload = {\n            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n            \"asset\": asset,\n            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n            \"time_length\": time_length,\n            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n            \"paths\": paths,\n        }\n        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        (PREDICTIONS_DIR / name).write_text(json.dumps(payload))\n        n += 1\n    return n\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, must be <= data_cutoff\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--num-simulations\",\n        type=int,\n        default=1000,\n        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n    )\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    start = end - timedelta(days=args.days)\n    # the context reaches back 7 days before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end)\n    n = generate(\n        args.asset,\n        start,\n        end,\n        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n        time_length=args.time_length,\n        num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n    )\n    print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n    result = backtest(\n        miner_name=\"campaign\",\n        asset=args.asset,\n        time_length=args.time_length,\n        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n        n_backtest_days=args.days,\n        predictions_dir=PREDICTIONS_DIR,\n        eval_end=end,\n    )\n    print(\"summary:\", result.summary)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '120,205p' agent/CAMPAIGN.md; cat DATA.md; cat pyproject.toml; cat agent/modeling.py; sed -n '1,85p' agent/predict.py; git status --short; env | sort | rg 'SYNTH|BUDGET|CAMPAIGN'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '120,205p' agent/CAMPAIGN.md; cat DATA.md; cat pyproject.toml; cat agent/modeling.py; sed -n '1,85p' agent/predict.py; git status --short; env | sort | rg 'SYNTH|BUDGET|CAMPAIGN'\"","aggregated_output":"  of historical field scores and rewards inside your snapshot — you do not need the API for\n  ranks, and the bundle covers your whole data window.\n- **synth-subnet** (a synth-lib dependency; source: github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet): the\n  validator's code. Read it to understand exactly how you'll be scored.\n- **Public Synth API** (api.synthdata.co): historical field scores\n  (`/validation/scores/historical`, query windows ≤ 2 days) and rewards (`/rewards/scores`).\n  synth-lib handles pagination for you. Studying the field (CRPS levels, what the top miners do)\n  is ALLOWED and recommended; dissecting the paths served by an individual miner in order to\n  copy them is FORBIDDEN.\n- **Miner dashboard analytics API** (`https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1`, schema at\n  `https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1/openapi.json`): the public backend behind the miner\n  dashboard — scoreboards, leaderboards, reward pools. Read the OpenAPI schema to discover the\n  endpoints. Same rule as the scores API: studying the field is encouraged, dissecting an\n  individual miner's served paths to copy them is not.\n- **Pretrained models & Hugging Face**: allowed and in scope. The sandbox has network access to\n  the HF Hub and PyPI; the GPU is yours and sits idle unless you use it. Time-series foundation\n  models, fine-tuning, or classical ML are all legitimate strategies — as is deciding, with\n  evidence, that they don't beat closed-form calibration. If you go this way: download weights\n  EARLY (bandwidth is part of your clock), set `HF_HOME` inside your workspace, and remember\n  your champion must run OFFLINE — weights must be committed to your git workspace, total under\n  a few GB (the harness collects your repo as a git bundle).\n- **Serving latency**: the live validator gives you roughly the prompt's lead time (~1 minute)\n  to respond — that is the hard bound. But the evaluation of your champion generates several\n  thousand prompts, and your own backtests will too: at more than a few seconds per prompt\n  (1000 paths, this hardware), your iteration loop and your evaluation both become the\n  bottleneck. Measure your per-prompt latency early and treat ~5 s as the practical ceiling.\n- **The web**: open for knowledge — searching the literature (arXiv, papers, reference\n  implementations) is encouraged — but NEVER for fetching prices or market data (see hard\n  rules).\n\n## Your envelope\n\n- Credit budget: 100.0 USD. Deadline: 18 h of wall-clock time.\n- The `BUDGET.md` file in your workspace is maintained by the harness: READ IT AT THE START OF\n  EACH ITERATION. When it contains a LANDING ORDER, it is non-negotiable.\n- Hardware: GCP g2-standard-16: 16 vCPU / 64GB RAM / 1x NVIDIA L4 (24GB VRAM). Your sandbox gets 14 CPU, 48GB RAM and the GPU. torch is already in your pyproject — no need to add it.. ONLY ONE GPU job at a time; cap the memory of your heavy jobs.\n- **You are expected to use your envelope.** Iterating is the job: measure, change one thing,\n  measure again. **Nominating is final** — the first time you stop while `agent/CHAMPION`\n  exists, your campaign is over: you will not be resumed, and every remaining dollar and hour\n  is forfeited. Until then you may keep iterating and amend your nomination. Nominate early\n  only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score.\n\n## Hard rules (violations = disqualification)\n\n1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at\n   `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat\n   everything after **2026-08-29** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards,\n   dashboard) for times after 2026-08-29 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and\n   disqualifies you. Audited on your transcript.\n2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges,\n   aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS/rank evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester`\n   (via `agent/predict.py`). This is what makes your work comparable to others'.\n4. Forbidden: falsifying the journal/results; fetching or dissecting predictions served by\n   individual miners.\n5. **ABSOLUTE prohibition on reading the operator's own private research code** (any\n   already-developed miner model outside your workspace). It should not exist anywhere in your\n   environment. If you come across it by any means whatsoever — a mount, a copy, an archive, a\n   search result — do not access it, do not read it, do not draw on it, and report it in\n   `suggestions.md`. Your work must start from public sources (synth-lib, synth-subnet, the\n   Synth API) and your own ideas.\n6. Your final champion must expose, in `agent/modeling.py`:\n   `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)`\n   -> tuple `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)` — each path: a list of\n   `time_length//time_increment + 1` floats starting at the last price in the context.\n   **The `context_prices` contract, exactly**: a minute-indexed pd.DataFrame over the 7 days\n   preceding `start_time`, with columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close`\n   is the series you are scored against; the rest are context. It MAY CONTAIN NaN in every\n   column — your `simulate()` must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate). Evaluation passes\n   the raw frame: handle gaps inside your model, not in a loader you hope evaluation shares.\n   Runnable OFFLINE (weights/artifacts committed or included in the workspace).\n\n## Required deliverables (in `agent/`)\n\nWrite `journal.md`, `report.md`, and `suggestions.md` in English — these reports are published\nto the Synth miner community.\n\n- `journal.md`: one entry per iteration — Hypothesis / Change / Result (numbers) / Verdict\n  (keep-discard) / Lesson. As you go: this is your memory if you crash.\n- `report.md`: your final report, explainer style (audience = Synth miners). Sections: context,\n  approach, experiments (failures included), results, limitations, what you'd do with more\n  budget.\n- `CHAMPION`: YAML — `sha` (an EXISTING git commit in your workspace, not a placeholder),\n  `agent_dir: agent`, `profiles`, `notes`. `profiles` must list the formats your champion\n  supports: `[low, high]` if you cover both 24h AND 1h (expected), `[low]` if you could only\n  handle the 24h. `notes` MUST include your champion's backtested rank per competition,\n# DATA.md — the shape of your market data (generated from THIS snapshot at setup)\n\nEach day is one parquet file, `date=YYYY-MM-DD.parquet`, a full 1440-row minute grid\nwith columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close` is the scored series.\nOnly `close` carries real data: the venue's 1-minute candle close (the last trade of\nthat minute). `open/high/low/volume` columns may exist but are NA in this snapshot.\n`source`/`ingested_at`/`is_final` are ingestion provenance — ignore them. Semantics:\n\n- **NaN close** = no trade that minute (thin market or feed gap). NOT market hours:\n  these venues trade 24/7. Real density varies by asset and era — see the table.\n- **Missing file** = before that market's first trade. Nothing existed; nothing is hidden.\n- Scoring drops NaN per prompt. Never interpolate: inventing prices in the gaps is how\n  you fool your own validation.\n\nPer-asset coverage, measured from this snapshot (nan% = share of NaN minutes among the\nasset's real days; first/last 30d columns show density drift — early months of newer\nlistings are genuinely thin, low realized volatility there is real):\n\n| asset | first day | last day | real days | nan% total | nan% first 30d | nan% last 30d |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AAPLX | 2025-11-21 | 2026-08-29 | 282 | 43.6% | 60.1% | 15.7% |\n| BTC | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| ETH | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| GOOGLX | 2025-11-18 | 2026-08-29 | 285 | 25.8% | 23.9% | 9.9% |\n| HYPE | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.1% | 0.1% | 0.0% |\n| NVDAX | 2025-11-12 | 2026-08-29 | 291 | 11.0% | 14.9% | 4.0% |\n| SOL | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| SP500 | 2026-03-18 | 2026-08-29 | 165 | 1.0% | 2.8% | 0.2% |\n| SPCX | 2026-05-17 | 2026-08-29 | 105 | 1.9% | 4.6% | 1.2% |\n| TSLAX | 2025-11-13 | 2026-08-29 | 290 | 14.9% | 26.2% | 12.4% |\n| WTIOIL | 2026-01-06 | 2026-08-29 | 236 | 13.2% | 58.8% | 1.9% |\n| XAU | 2025-12-22 | 2026-08-29 | 251 | 11.2% | 39.2% | 1.5% |\n| XRP | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n[project]\nname = \"campaign-workspace\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.12,<3.14\"\ndependencies = [\"synth-lib\", \"numpy>=2.2\", \"pandas>=2.3\", \"torch>=2.0\"]\n\n[tool.uv.sources]\nsynth-lib = { git = \"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib\", rev = \"782a44fe7585a4e7b0388e22b99c57f13d56f5ee\" }\n\"\"\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.\n\nThis is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.\nContract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has\ntime_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef simulate(\n    asset: str,\n    start_time,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n    context_prices=None,\n):\n    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1\n    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].dropna()\n    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\n    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\n    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0\n    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])\n\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n\nUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\nGenerates predictions from agent/modeling.py over a grid of past prompts (covered by the\nsnapshot), writes them in the standard format, then scores them with backtest() (validator\nCRPS + rank vs the real field via the Synth API).\n\n--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\ngeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\nfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import OHLCV_COLUMNS, STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.market_data import MinutePriceStore\n\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n\nfrom modeling import simulate  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n\nCONTEXT_MINUTES = 7 * 24 * 60\nPREDICTIONS_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\" / \"predictions\"\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n\n    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n\n\ndef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n\n    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n\n\ndef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n\n    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(asset)\n    missing = []\n    cursor = start.date()\n    while cursor <= end.date():\n        if not (root / f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\").exists():\n            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only) and stops at the campaign's data_cutoff. \"\n            f\"Reduce --eval-end / --days to stay within the available coverage ({root}).\"\n        )\n\n\ndef generate(\n    asset: str,\n?? agent/BUDGET.md\n?? uv.lock\nSYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT=/workspace/market_data/offline_data\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
