{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/predict.py\n@@\n from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest\n+from synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\n@@\n PREDICTIONS_DIR = WORKSPACE / \\\"miner_outputs\\\" / \\\"campaign\\\" / \\\"predictions\\\"\n+CUTOFF = pd.Timestamp(\\\"2026-08-29\\\", tz=\\\"UTC\\\")\n+\n+\n+def load_context(asset, start, end):\n+    check_snapshot_coverage(asset, start, end)\n+    frames = []\n+    for day in pd.date_range(start.date(), end.date(), freq=\\\"D\\\"):\n+        frames.append(pd.read_parquet(store_root(asset) / f\\\"date={day.date()}.parquet\\\"))\n+    frame = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n+    frame[\\\"timestamp\\\"] = pd.to_datetime(frame[\\\"timestamp\\\"], utc=True)\n+    return frame.drop_duplicates(\\\"timestamp\\\").set_index(\\\"timestamp\\\").sort_index().reindex(columns=OHLCV_COLUMNS).loc[start:end]\n@@\n def check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> None:\n@@\n-    root = store_root(asset)\n+    if pd.Timestamp(end) > CUTOFF:\n+        raise ValueError(\\\"Evaluation must end no later than 2026-08-29 00:00 UTC\\\")\n+    root = store_root(asset)\n@@\n     num_simulations: int = 1000,\n+    predictions_dir: Path = PREDICTIONS_DIR,\n ) -> int:\n-    store = MinutePriceStore(asset, root=store_root(asset))\n-    df = store.load_range(start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end).set_index(\\\"timestamp\\\")\n-    prices = df[OHLCV_COLUMNS]\n-    PREDICTIONS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n-    end_ts = pd.Timestamp(end)\n+    scores = get_miner_scores(start, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n+    times = pd.DatetimeIndex(scores[\\\"start_time\\\"].unique()).sort_values()\n+    if times.empty:\n+        raise ValueError(\\\"No archived prompts in requested window\\\")\n+    prices = load_context(asset, times.min() - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), times.max())\n+    check_snapshot_coverage(asset, times.min(), min(pd.Timestamp(end), times.max() + pd.Timedelta(hours=26)))\n+    predictions_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n     n = 0\n-    for t in pd.date_range(start, end, freq=f\\\"{cadence_minutes}min\\\", tz=\\\"UTC\\\"):\n-        if t >= end_ts:\n-            break\n-        context = prices.loc[:t][-CONTEXT_MINUTES:]\n+    for t in times:\n+        context = prices.loc[(prices.index > t - pd.Timedelta(days=7)) & (prices.index <= t)]\n@@\n-        (PREDICTIONS_DIR / name).write_text(json.dumps(payload))\n+        (predictions_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(payload))\n@@\n     ap.add_argument(\\\"--eval-end\\\", required=True, help=\\\"YYYY-MM-DD, must be <= data_cutoff\\\")\n+    ap.add_argument(\\\"--run-name\\\", default=\\\"campaign\\\")\n@@\n     start = end - timedelta(days=args.days)\n+    predictions_dir = WORKSPACE / \\\"miner_outputs\\\" / args.run_name / \\\"predictions\\\"\n@@\n         num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n+        predictions_dir=predictions_dir,\n@@\n-        miner_name=\\\"campaign\\\",\n+        miner_name=args.run_name,\n@@\n-        predictions_dir=PREDICTIONS_DIR,\n+        predictions_dir=predictions_dir,\n@@\n     print(\\\"summary:\\\", result.summary)\n+    output_dir = AGENT_DIR / \\\"results\\\" / args.run_name\n+    output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n+    label = f\\\"{args.asset}_{args.time_length}\\\"\n+    result.prompt_df.to_parquet(output_dir / f\\\"{label}_prompts.parquet\\\")\n+    result.smoothed_scores.to_parquet(output_dir / f\\\"{label}_smoothed.parquet\\\")\n+    (output_dir / f\\\"{label}_summary.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps(result.summary, indent=2))\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n+# Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 0 — preregistration and evaluation audit\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the seven-day Gaussian starter is miscalibrated in changing volatility regimes; correcting evaluation mechanics must precede model comparisons.\n+- Change: installed the pinned public libraries with \"'`uv sync`; read the validator'\"'s CRPS, competition configuration, weighting and official backtester. Replaced the starter's strict context loader with raw parquet loading, preserving NaNs. Generate at archived prompt timestamps rather than approximate hourly timestamps. Enforce the frozen cutoff and separate candidate output directories.\n+- Result: pending baseline. Snapshot contains 13 live assets; both 289-point and 61-point formats require 1000 served paths. The daily score sums 288 five-minute, 48 thirty-minute, 8 three-hour changes and one absolute endpoint; the hourly score additionally includes twelve start-to-horizon gap terms.\n+- Verdict: keep infrastructure changes, not a model claim.\n+- Lesson: the campaign describes a lenient starter loader, but the provided implementation actually calls strict \"'`load_range`. Also, installed competition windows are 10 days (daily) and 5 days (hourly), not a 24-hour window; use the pinned validator as truth.\n+\n+## Research protocol\n+\n+All prices come from the snapshot. Never inspect data after 2026-08-29 or individual miners'\"' served predictions. Training targets end before validation starts. Field comparisons start after 2026-06-23; SP500 ranks only after 2026-07-19. Initial development windows: scored 2026-07-20 to 2026-07-30 and 2026-08-04 to 2026-08-14; reserve 2026-08-18 to 2026-08-28 for final validation. Inspect volatility to determine whether those regimes genuinely differ rather than asserting they do.\n+\n+Planned sequence: reproducible baseline; recent versus seven-day volatility; robust scale and heavy-tailed mixtures; horizon-dependent volatility reversion; fitted volatility forecasting if simpler calibration stalls. Each substantive change needs lower paired official CRPS across both development windows (target at least 0.5% mean gain), no competition-level regression exceeding 1%, and final field-relative validation at 1000 paths. These are provisional selection gates, not claims of statistical significance. All CRPS and reward calculations use \"'`synth_lib.backtester` functions through `agent/predict.py`.\n*** Update File: agent/suggestions.md\n@@\n+# Suggestions and infrastructure observations\n+\n+- The starter `predict.py` uses strict `MinutePriceStore.load_range`, despite campaign text describing it as a sanctioned lenient example. Read raw partitions for context so legitimate NaNs remain intact.\n+- Campaign prose calls smoothing 24 hours; the pinned competition config specifies 10-day daily and 5-day hourly scoring windows. Report the implemented windows explicitly.\n+- `DATA.md` says only close is populated, but inspected BTC partitions also contain real OHLCV and trade-count values. The model will depend only on close so this discrepancy cannot affect portability.\n+- No operator-private research code has been encountered or used.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-30 --num-simulations 256 --run-name starter_probe > /workspace/agent/baseline_probe.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
