{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/research.py\n@@\n     schedule = None\n     learned_scale = 1.0\n+    innovation = parts[0] if parts[0] in [\\\"iid\\\", \\\"sv\\\", \\\"boot\\\"] else None\n+    innovation_parameters = parts[1:]\n+    if innovation:\n+        parts = [\\\"auto\\\", \\\"0\\\", \\\"1\\\"]\n@@\n     shocks = np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:count]\n+    if innovation == \\\"iid\\\":\n+        degrees = float(innovation_parameters[0])\n+        shocks *= np.sqrt((degrees - 2) / rng.chisquare(degrees, size=shocks.shape))\n+    elif innovation == \\\"sv\\\":\n+        spread, persistence = map(float, innovation_parameters)\n+        correlation = np.exp(-increment / 60 / persistence)\n+        state = rng.standard_normal(count) * spread\n+        for step in range(steps):\n+            state = correlation * state + np.sqrt(1-correlation**2) * spread * rng.standard_normal(count)\n+            shocks[:,step] *= np.exp(state-spread**2)\n+    elif innovation == \\\"boot\\\":\n+        empirical = feature['returns']\n+        sampled = rng.choice(empirical, size=shocks.shape)\n+        sampled = sampled - np.mean(empirical)\n+        shocks = sampled / max(np.std(empirical), 1e-9)\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n ### Iteration 4 result\n@@\n Volatility reversion does not clear the paired >0.5% gate. The conservative 6h target/1h reversion has mean relative ratios COM_EQU_24H 0.9995/0.9990, hourly 0.9987/0.9997, daily crypto 0.9999/0.9998. Longer reversion to 24h helps the calm window but hurts the earlier volatile window. Discard for now: the flat horizon-specific robust scale is simpler and comparably calibrated.\n+\n+## Iteration 6 — temporal organization of heavy tails (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: tails generated independently at each step or by evolving stochastic volatility may match multi-horizon scoring better than one constant latent scale per path.\n+- Change: compare iid Student innovations (df 3/5/8), lognormal stochastic volatility (log-scale SD 0.4/0.7, persistence 1h/6h), and mean-centered empirical-return bootstrap to the incumbent pathwise df=5 model. Keep RMS diffusion scale fixed; this screen diagnoses distribution shape, not a final parameter search.\n+- Result: pending; two development windows, 256 paths, identical prompt sample.\n+- Verdict: pending; require consistent gains to justify the added path dynamics.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/research.py --name dynamics_screen --variants auto:0:1:5,iid:3,iid:5,iid:8,sv:0.4:60,sv:0.7:60,sv:0.4:360,sv:0.7:360,boot:0 --workers 4 > agent/dynamics_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
