{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: agent/fit_clock.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Fit strictly positive intraday variance-shape priors from pre-field prices.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import json\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+from predict import AGENT_DIR, load_context, store_root\n+from research import CRYPTO,EQUITY\n+\n+profiles={}\n+for asset in CRYPTO+EQUITY:\n+    first=sorted(store_root(asset).glob('date=*.parquet'))[0].stem.removeprefix('date=')\n+    start=max(pd.Timestamp(first,tz='UTC'),pd.Timestamp('2026-04-01',tz='UTC'))\n+    close=load_context(asset,start,pd.Timestamp('2026-07-26',tz='UTC')).close.dropna()\n+    gaps=np.diff(close.index.as_unit('ns').asi8)/60e9\n+    absolute=np.abs(np.diff(np.log(close.to_numpy(dtype=float))))/np.sqrt(gaps)\n+    frame=pd.DataFrame({'absolute':absolute,'day':close.index[1:].date,'hour':close.index[1:].hour})\n+    frame['relative']=frame.absolute/frame.groupby('day').absolute.transform('mean').clip(lower=1e-9)\n+    profile=frame.groupby('hour').relative.mean().reindex(range(24),fill_value=1).to_numpy()\n+    profile=.25*np.roll(profile,1)+.5*profile+.25*np.roll(profile,-1)\n+    profile=np.clip(profile,.25,3)\n+    profiles[asset]=profile/profile.mean()\n+    print(asset,profile.min(),profile.max(),flush=True)\n+np.savez(AGENT_DIR/'clock_profiles.npz',**profiles)\n+(AGENT_DIR/'clock_profiles.json').write_text(json.dumps({'fitting_start':'2026-04-01 or first available trade','fitting_end':'2026-07-26','interpretation':'Positive hourly volatility shape only; no market-closure/calendar rules.'},indent=2))\n*** Update File: agent/research.py\n@@\n-    for half_life in [30, 60, 180, 360, 720, 1440, 2880, 10080]:\n+    for half_life in [15, 30, 60, 120, 180, 360, 720, 1440, 2880, 10080]:\n@@\n def generate_variant(feature, asset, start_time, increment, length, count, variant):\n@@\n     parts = variant.split(\\\":\\\")\n+    prior_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0] == 'prior' else 0.\n+    if parts[0] == 'quick':\n+        parts = ['av',parts[1],'1','5']\n@@\n     cycle_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0] == \\\"cycle\\\" else 0.\n+    if prior_strength:\n+        cycle_strength = .75\n+        parts = ['hybrid','1']\n@@\n     if cycle_strength and length > 3600:\n         future_times = pd.Timestamp(start_time) + pd.to_timedelta(np.arange(1,steps+1)*increment,unit='s')\n-        sigma *= 1 + cycle_strength*(feature['cycle'][future_times.hour]-1)\n+        profile = feature['cycle']\n+        if prior_strength:\n+            with np.load(AGENT_DIR/'clock_profiles.npz') as archive:\n+                profile = (1-prior_strength)*profile + prior_strength*archive[asset]\n+        sigma *= 1 + cycle_strength*(profile[future_times.hour]-1)\n@@\n     parser.add_argument(\\\"--workers\\\", type=int, default=10)\n+    parser.add_argument(\\\"--format\\\", choices=['all','low','high'],default='all')\n@@\n-             for length in ([86400, 3600] if asset in CRYPTO else [86400])]\n+             for length in ([86400, 3600] if asset in CRYPTO else [86400])\n+             if args.format=='all' or (args.format=='low' and length==86400) or (args.format=='high' and length==3600)]\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n ## Iteration 10 — moment-matched tail calibration (preregistered)\n@@\n - Lesson: pending.\n+\n+### Iteration 10 result\n+\n+Moment matching does not reveal a consistent material improvement. Student df3 at matched absolute scale 1.0 gives hourly 0.99920/0.99939 but daily-crypto 1.00044/1.00166; other scale choices trade gains in the calmer window for losses in the earlier window. Retain df5 at the existing scale. This confirms that the prior simple mixture was near a broad calibration optimum; it does not prove all heavy-tailed models are equivalent.\n+\n+## Iteration 11 — periodic-profile stability (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: six or seven observed days make the local variance profile noisy. A strictly pre-field historical profile can regularize it without any assumed exchange calendar or zero-variance periods.\n+- Change: fit positive per-asset hourly profiles from April 1 (or first trade) through July 26, using the same within-day normalization and circular smoothing. Blend 25/50/75/100% historical prior into the local profile; keep total cycle strength 0.75. Separately check 15/30/60/120-minute robust half-lives for hourly forecasts, changing nothing else.\n+- Result: pending official development-window CRPS. The historical profile never reads validation-period prices when fitted.\n+- Verdict: require consistent gains across both windows; otherwise prefer the local-only profile and 60-minute hourly scale.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/fit_clock.py > agent/fit_clock.log 2>&1 && uv run agent/research.py --name clock_prior_screen --variants cycle:0.75,prior:0.25,prior:0.5,prior:0.75,prior:1 --format low --workers 4 > agent/clock_prior_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
