{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: agent/refit_vol.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Refit the fixed likelihood architecture using all pre-validation labels.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import json\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+import torch\n+from torch import nn\n+\n+from predict import AGENT_DIR\n+\n+print((AGENT_DIR/'BUDGET.md').read_text(),flush=True)\n+torch.set_num_threads(4)\n+device='cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n+if device=='cuda':\n+    torch.cuda.set_per_process_memory_fraction(.35)\n+data=np.load(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'volatility_training.npz')\n+previous=dict(np.load(AGENT_DIR/'volatility_weights.npz'))\n+values=np.clip((data['inputs']-previous['center'])/previous['spread'],-8,8)\n+age=(pd.Timestamp('2026-07-26',tz='UTC').value-data['timestamps'])/86400e9\n+inputs=torch.tensor(values,dtype=torch.float32,device=device)\n+targets=torch.tensor(np.clip(data['targets'],.02,20),dtype=torch.float32,device=device)\n+for name,half_life in [('uniform',None),('recent60',60),('recent120',120)]:\n+    torch.manual_seed(95)\n+    weights=np.ones(len(age)) if half_life is None else np.exp(-np.log(2)*age/half_life)\n+    weights=weights/weights.mean()\n+    weight_tensor=torch.tensor(weights,dtype=torch.float32,device=device)\n+    network=nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(values.shape[1],48),nn.SiLU(),nn.Linear(48,32),nn.SiLU(),nn.Linear(32,2)).to(device)\n+    network.load_state_dict({key:torch.tensor(previous[key],device=device) for key in network.state_dict()})\n+    optimizer=torch.optim.AdamW(network.parameters(),lr=.0005,weight_decay=.02)\n+    for epoch in range(40):\n+        order=torch.randperm(len(inputs),device=device)\n+        for batch in order.split(1024):\n+            output=network(inputs[batch]).clamp(-2,2)\n+            loss=((targets[batch]*torch.exp(-output)+output+.03*output.square()).mean(dim=1)*weight_tensor[batch]).mean()\n+            optimizer.zero_grad()\n+            loss.backward()\n+            optimizer.step()\n+    state={key:value.detach().cpu().numpy().copy() for key,value in network.state_dict().items()}\n+    np.savez(AGENT_DIR/f'refit_{name}_weights.npz',center=previous['center'],spread=previous['spread'],ridge=previous['ridge'],**state)\n+    metadata={'contexts':len(inputs),'target_cutoff':'2026-07-26','recency_half_life_days':half_life,'epochs':40,'initialization':'Original likelihood model','last_batch_training_loss':float(loss.detach().cpu())}\n+    (AGENT_DIR/f'refit_{name}_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metadata,indent=2))\n+    print(name,metadata,flush=True)\n*** Update File: agent/research.py\n@@\n-@lru_cache(maxsize=2)\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=8)\n def learned_weights(kind='neural'):\n     filename = 'score_weights.npz' if kind == 'curve' else 'volatility_weights.npz'\n+    if kind.startswith('refit_'):\n+        filename = f'{kind}_weights.npz'\n@@\n     prior_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0] == 'prior' else 0.\n+    refit_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0] == 'refit' else None\n@@\n     if prior_strength:\n@@\n         parts = ['hybrid','1']\n+    if refit_parameters:\n+        cycle_strength = .75\n+        parts = ['auto','0','1','5'] if length == 3600 else ['ml','refit_'+refit_parameters[0],refit_parameters[1]]\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n ## Iteration 11 — periodic-profile stability (preregistered)\n@@\n - Lesson: pending.\n+\n+### Iteration 11 result\n+\n+Keep local-only profile and 60-minute hourly memory. Historical profile shrinkage has <0.1% gains and mixed COM_EQU performance (100% prior 0.99930/1.00120). Hourly 15/30/120-minute half-lives versus 60-minute produce 1.00186/1.00422, 1.00008/1.00028, and 1.00135/1.00211. The additional parameters are not justified.\n+\n+## Iteration 12 — chronological refitting and recency weighting (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the original network's optimizer only fitted labels before July 1; July 1–25 was used for model selection. Refitting on all labels already available before the field windows, with recency weighting, may better match newer venues without violating no-lookahead.\n+- Change: initialize from the likelihood model, make 40 fixed-epoch passes over all pre-July-26 labels, and compare uniform versus 60/120-day exponential recency weights. No development or final-window labels enter the fit. Daily correction remains full strength with the 0.75 local profile; hourly stays classical. Compare optional half-strength shrinkage only if full corrections regress.\n+- Result: pending official development-window CRPS. Training-batch likelihood is only diagnostic, not evidence of improvement.\n+- Verdict: keep only a consistent cross-window gain; otherwise retain the original frozen weights.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/refit_vol.py > agent/refit_vol.log 2>&1 && uv run agent/research.py --name refit_screen --variants cycle:0.75,refit:uniform:1,refit:recent60:1,refit:recent120:1 --format low --workers 6 > agent/refit_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/predict.py\n@@\n     predictions_dir: Path = PREDICTIONS_DIR,\n+    simulator=simulate,\n@@\n-        out = simulate(\n+        out = simulator(\n*** Add File: agent/field_eval.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Full-path official backtests and cross-asset validator reward aggregation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+import json\n+import shutil\n+from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\n+from functools import partial\n+\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+from predict import AGENT_DIR, WORKSPACE, backtest, ensure_workspace_cwd, generate\n+from research import CRYPTO, EQUITY, WINDOWS, features, generate_variant\n+from synth_lib.backtester.config import competition_for, slug_for\n+from synth_lib.backtester.result import BacktestResult\n+from synth_lib.backtester.scoring import compute_combined_smoothed_scores\n+\n+\n+def variant_simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices, variant):\n+    feature = features(context_prices, start_time, time_increment)\n+    paths = generate_variant(feature, asset, pd.Timestamp(start_time), time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, variant)\n+    return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\n+\n+\n+def evaluate(task):\n+    asset, length, window, variant, name = task\n+    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n+    begin, end = [pd.Timestamp(value, tz=\\\"UTC\\\").to_pydatetime() for value in WINDOWS[window]]\n+    increment = 60 if length == 3600 else 300\n+    label = f\\\"{asset}_{length}\\\"\n+    output = AGENT_DIR / \\\"results\\\" / name / window\n+    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n+    if (output / f\\\"{label}_summary.json\\\").exists():\n+        return str(output), label\n+    predictions = WORKSPACE / \\\"miner_outputs\\\" / name / window / label / \\\"predictions\\\"\n+    kwargs = {} if variant == \\\"model\\\" else {\\\"simulator\\\": partial(variant_simulate, variant=variant)}\n+    total = generate(asset, begin, end, time_increment=increment, time_length=length,\n+                     num_simulations=1000, predictions_dir=predictions, **kwargs)\n+    print(f\\\"Generated {total} {label} {window}\\\", flush=True)\n+    result = backtest(miner_name=name, asset=asset, time_length=length, time_increment=increment,\n+                      n_backtest_days=(end-begin).days, predictions_dir=predictions, eval_end=end)\n+    result.prompt_df.to_parquet(output / f\\\"{label}_prompts.parquet\\\")\n+    result.smoothed_scores.to_parquet(output / f\\\"{label}_smoothed.parquet\\\")\n+    (output / f\\\"{label}_summary.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps(result.summary, indent=2))\n+    shutil.rmtree(predictions)\n+    return str(output), label\n+\n+\n+def reward_summary(frame):\n+    totals = frame.groupby(\\\"miner_uid\\\").reward_weight.sum()\n+    latest = frame.loc[frame.updated_at.eq(frame.updated_at.max())].set_index(\\\"miner_uid\\\")\n+    return {\\\"reward_rank\\\": int(totals.rank(ascending=False, method=\\\"min\\\").loc[999]),\n+            \\\"final_rank\\\": int(latest.new_smoothed_score.rank(method=\\\"min\\\").loc[999]),\n+            \\\"miners\\\": int(len(totals)), \\\"reward_ratio\\\": float(totals.loc[999] / totals.drop(999).max()),\n+            \\\"reward_rounds\\\": int(frame.updated_at.nunique()),\n+            \\\"first_round\\\": str(frame.updated_at.min()), \\\"last_round\\\": str(frame.updated_at.max())}\n+\n+\n+def aggregate(name, window):\n+    output = AGENT_DIR / \\\"results\\\" / name / window\n+    competition_groups = {}\n+    for path in sorted(output.glob('*_summary.json')):\n+        label = path.name.removesuffix('_summary.json')\n+        asset, length = label.rsplit('_', 1)\n+        config = competition_for(asset, int(length))\n+        result = BacktestResult(name, pd.read_parquet(output / f'{label}_prompts.parquet'),\n+                                pd.read_parquet(output / f'{label}_smoothed.parquet'), json.loads(path.read_text()))\n+        competition_groups.setdefault(slug_for(config), (config, []))[1].append(result)\n+    summaries = {}\n+    for label, (config, results) in competition_groups.items():\n+        combined = compute_combined_smoothed_scores(results, config)\n+        combined.to_parquet(output / f'{label}_combined.parquet')\n+        summaries[label] = reward_summary(combined)\n+        summaries[label]['assets'] = len(results)\n+        print(label, summaries[label], flush=True)\n+    summaries['score_estimate'] = 100 * sum(min(1, value['reward_ratio']) for value in summaries.values()) / 3\n+    (output / 'competition_metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(summaries, indent=2))\n+    return summaries\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument('--name', required=True)\n+    parser.add_argument('--variant', default='model')\n+    parser.add_argument('--windows', default='dev1,dev2')\n+    parser.add_argument('--assets', default=','.join(CRYPTO + EQUITY))\n+    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=6)\n+    parser.add_argument('--aggregate-only', action='store_true')\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+    print((AGENT_DIR / 'BUDGET.md').read_text(), flush=True)\n+    if not args.aggregate_only:\n+        tasks = [(asset, length, window, args.variant, args.name)\n+                 for window in args.windows.split(',') for asset in args.assets.split(',')\n+                 for length in ([86400, 3600] if asset in CRYPTO else [86400])]\n+        with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.workers) as executor:\n+            list(executor.map(evaluate, tasks))\n+    for window in args.windows.split(','):\n+        print(aggregate(args.name, window), flush=True)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == '__main__':\n+    main()\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n - Lesson: pending.\n+\n+### Iteration 1 result\n+\n+Official CRPS screening uses 60 prompts per asset/format/window (2160 prompts total), 256 paths, five candidates. Six-hour absolute-return scale versus deterministic starter: mean asset-relative CRPS ratios are dev1/dev2 0.9750/0.9002 for COM_EQU_24H, 0.9729/0.9438 for CRYPTO_1H, and 0.9933/0.9761 for CRYPTO_24H. It is the best hourly variant for all five crypto assets in both windows. Keep robust recent scale as the next baseline. The windows differ materially in calibration improvement, although this alone does not establish opposite market regimes. Full official 1000-path field replays are starting; reduced-path averages are not emission estimates.\n+\n+## Iteration 2 — scale and mixture calibration (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: absolute-return scaling still understates the peaked, heavy-tailed return distribution. A pathwise variance mixture can improve both near-zero sharpness and tail coverage without a directional forecast.\n+- Change: screen 1h/3h/6h/12h absolute-return half-lives, then multiplier and Student-t path-scale grids against av:360. Do not change multiple dimensions in the first half-life experiment.\n+- Result: pending; retain candidates only if both development windows improve by at least 0.5% or a competition improves without a >1% regression elsewhere.\n+- Verdict: pending.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/field_eval.py --name starter_full --variant starter --windows dev1,dev2 > agent/starter_full.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
