{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .gitignore\n@@\n market_data/\n+agent/BUDGET.md\n+agent/*.log\n+agent/results/**/*_prompts.parquet\n+agent/results/**/*_smoothed.parquet\n+agent/results/**/*_combined.parquet\n+agent/results/volatility_training.npz\n+agent/results/training_score_curves.npz\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n ## Iteration 9 — empirical periodic volatility, not sessions (preregistered)\n@@\n - Lesson: pending.\n+\n+### Iteration 9 result\n+\n+The empirical positive volatility profile clears the gate. Relative to the daily-neural incumbent, strength 0.75 gives COM_EQU_24H 0.98653/0.98038 and daily crypto 0.99567/0.99463; strength 1 gives 0.98496/0.97800 and 0.99577/0.99467. Hourly is unchanged. Thus continuous trading does not imply a flat variance clock in this snapshot. Prefer the slightly shrunk 0.75 profile provisionally and validate full field emissions at 1000 paths; do not reinterpret this as exchange-session closures.\n+\n+### Iteration 8 training result\n+\n+Computed 95,750 official CRPS values at 128 paths over 6,081 pre-field contexts, with 9,575 valid context/horizon pairs. Score-aware fine-tuning improves the chronological interpolated validation ratio only from 0.992970 to 0.992561, peaking at epoch 5; longer fitting overfits. The new model is now undergoing fresh official development-window CRPS screening. This tiny training gain alone does not justify deployment.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ngit add .gitignore agent/modeling.py agent/predict.py agent/research.py agent/train_vol.py agent/fit_score_curves.py agent/rank_screen.py agent/journal.md agent/volatility_weights.npz agent/volatility_weights.json agent/score_weights.npz agent/score_weights.json agent/results/*.parquet agent/results/*ranks.json agent/results/invalid_training_units.json\ngit -c user.name='Campaign Research Agent' -c user.email='campaign-agent@localhost' commit -m \\\"Validate robust neural volatility and score-aligned research alternatives\\\"\nuv run agent/field_eval.py --name neural_cycle_full --variant cycle:0.75 --windows dev1,dev2 --workers 6 > agent/neural_cycle_full.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"[master 2348260] Validate robust neural volatility and score-aligned research alternatives\n 24 files changed, 808 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 agent/fit_score_curves.py\n create mode 100644 agent/rank_screen.py\n create mode 100644 agent/results/cycle_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/dense_confirmation.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/dense_confirmation_sampled_ranks.json\n create mode 100644 agent/results/dynamics_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/half_life_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/invalid_training_units.json\n create mode 100644 agent/results/learned_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/reversion_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/sampling_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/scale_mixture_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/score_fit_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/results/volatility_screen.parquet\n create mode 100644 agent/score_weights.json\n create mode 100644 agent/score_weights.npz\n create mode 100644 agent/train_vol.py\n create mode 100644 agent/volatility_weights.json\n create mode 100644 agent/volatility_weights.npz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
