{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '128,175p' agent/CAMPAIGN.md; sed -n '1,240p' agent/rank_screen.py; sed -n '1,220p' agent/modeling.py; sed -n '1,200p' agent/field_eval.py; sed -n '1,180p' agent/research.py; cat .gitignore\"","aggregated_output":"  copy them is FORBIDDEN.\n- **Miner dashboard analytics API** (`https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1`, schema at\n  `https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1/openapi.json`): the public backend behind the miner\n  dashboard — scoreboards, leaderboards, reward pools. Read the OpenAPI schema to discover the\n  endpoints. Same rule as the scores API: studying the field is encouraged, dissecting an\n  individual miner's served paths to copy them is not.\n- **Pretrained models & Hugging Face**: allowed and in scope. The sandbox has network access to\n  the HF Hub and PyPI; the GPU is yours and sits idle unless you use it. Time-series foundation\n  models, fine-tuning, or classical ML are all legitimate strategies — as is deciding, with\n  evidence, that they don't beat closed-form calibration. If you go this way: download weights\n  EARLY (bandwidth is part of your clock), set `HF_HOME` inside your workspace, and remember\n  your champion must run OFFLINE — weights must be committed to your git workspace, total under\n  a few GB (the harness collects your repo as a git bundle).\n- **Serving latency**: the live validator gives you roughly the prompt's lead time (~1 minute)\n  to respond — that is the hard bound. But the evaluation of your champion generates several\n  thousand prompts, and your own backtests will too: at more than a few seconds per prompt\n  (1000 paths, this hardware), your iteration loop and your evaluation both become the\n  bottleneck. Measure your per-prompt latency early and treat ~5 s as the practical ceiling.\n- **The web**: open for knowledge — searching the literature (arXiv, papers, reference\n  implementations) is encouraged — but NEVER for fetching prices or market data (see hard\n  rules).\n\n## Your envelope\n\n- Credit budget: 100.0 USD. Deadline: 18 h of wall-clock time.\n- The `BUDGET.md` file in your workspace is maintained by the harness: READ IT AT THE START OF\n  EACH ITERATION. When it contains a LANDING ORDER, it is non-negotiable.\n- Hardware: GCP g2-standard-16: 16 vCPU / 64GB RAM / 1x NVIDIA L4 (24GB VRAM). Your sandbox gets 14 CPU, 48GB RAM and the GPU. torch is already in your pyproject — no need to add it.. ONLY ONE GPU job at a time; cap the memory of your heavy jobs.\n- **You are expected to use your envelope.** Iterating is the job: measure, change one thing,\n  measure again. **Nominating is final** — the first time you stop while `agent/CHAMPION`\n  exists, your campaign is over: you will not be resumed, and every remaining dollar and hour\n  is forfeited. Until then you may keep iterating and amend your nomination. Nominate early\n  only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score.\n\n## Hard rules (violations = disqualification)\n\n1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at\n   `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat\n   everything after **2026-08-29** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards,\n   dashboard) for times after 2026-08-29 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and\n   disqualifies you. Audited on your transcript.\n2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges,\n   aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS/rank evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester`\n   (via `agent/predict.py`). This is what makes your work comparable to others'.\n4. Forbidden: falsifying the journal/results; fetching or dissecting predictions served by\n   individual miners.\n5. **ABSOLUTE prohibition on reading the operator's own private research code** (any\n\"\"\"Sampled end-of-window official reward ranks; not a full emission replay.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom predict import AGENT_DIR, replay_prompt_scores, parallel_combined, ensure_workspace_cwd\nfrom research import WINDOWS\nfrom field_eval import reward_summary\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import competition_for, slug_for\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.result import BacktestResult\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.scoring import compute_combined_smoothed_scores\n\n\ndef main():\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('experiment')\n    parser.add_argument('--template')\n    parser.add_argument('--round-step',type=int,default=1)\n    parser.add_argument('--workers',type=int,default=4)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    frame = pd.read_parquet(AGENT_DIR/'results'/f'{args.experiment}.parquet')\n    summaries = {}\n    for window, window_frame in frame.groupby('window'):\n        begin,end = [pd.Timestamp(value,tz='UTC') for value in WINDOWS[window]]\n        fields = {}\n        for (asset,length),group in window_frame.groupby(['asset','length']):\n            increment = 60 if length == 3600 else 300\n            field = get_miner_scores(begin,end,asset,int(length),increment)\n            fields[(asset,length)] = field.loc[field.start_time.isin(group.time.unique())]\n        for variant,variant_frame in window_frame.groupby('variant'):\n            groups = {}\n            for (asset,length),rows in variant_frame.groupby(['asset','length']):\n                config = competition_for(asset,int(length))\n                candidate = rows[['time','crps']].rename(columns={'time':'start_time'}).copy()\n                candidate['scored_time'] = candidate.start_time + pd.Timedelta(seconds=int(length))\n                candidate['miner_uid'] = 999\n                candidate['asset'] = asset\n                candidate['time_length'] = int(length)\n                candidate['time_increment'] = config.time_increment\n                scored = replay_prompt_scores(fields[(asset,length)],candidate)\n                rounds = pd.DataFrame({'updated_at':[end-pd.Timedelta(seconds=1)]})\n                if args.template:\n                    source = AGENT_DIR/'results'/args.template/window/f'{asset}_{length}_smoothed.parquet'\n                    rounds = pd.read_parquet(source,columns=['updated_at']).drop_duplicates().sort_values('updated_at').iloc[::args.round_step]\n                result = BacktestResult(variant,scored,rounds,{})\n                groups.setdefault(slug_for(config),(config,[]))[1].append(result)\n            for slug,(config,results) in groups.items():\n                combined = parallel_combined(results,config,workers=args.workers)\n                summary = reward_summary(combined)\n                key = f'{window}/{variant}/{slug}'\n                summaries[key] = summary\n                print(key,summary,flush=True)\n    suffix = 'sampled_ranks' if not args.template else f'template_step{args.round_step}_ranks'\n    (AGENT_DIR/'results'/f'{args.experiment}_{suffix}.json').write_text(json.dumps(summaries,indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    main()\n\"\"\"Offline probabilistic paths with robust, horizon-specific volatility forecasts.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nASSETS = (\"BTC\", \"ETH\", \"SOL\", \"XRP\", \"HYPE\", \"XAU\", \"NVDAX\", \"GOOGLX\", \"TSLAX\", \"AAPLX\", \"WTIOIL\", \"SPCX\", \"SP500\")\nHALF_LIVES = (30, 60, 180, 360, 720, 1440, 2880, 10080)\nCOMMODITY_EQUITY_BLEND = 1.0\nCYCLE_STRENGTH = 0.75\nWEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM = pd.Timestamp('2026-07-26',tz='UTC')\n\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef _weights():\n    with np.load(Path(__file__).with_name(\"volatility_weights.npz\"), allow_pickle=False) as archive:\n        return {name: archive[name] for name in archive.files}\n\n\ndef _features(closes, timestamp):\n    minutes = (closes.index - timestamp).total_seconds().to_numpy() / 60\n    gaps = np.diff(minutes)\n    returns = np.diff(np.log(closes.to_numpy(dtype=float)))\n    valid = (gaps > 0) & np.isfinite(returns)\n    normalized = returns[valid] / np.sqrt(gaps[valid])\n    age = -minutes[1:][valid]\n    absolute, root_square = {}, {}\n    for half_life in HALF_LIVES:\n        if not normalized.size:\n            absolute[half_life] = root_square[half_life] = 1e-8\n            continue\n        weights = np.exp(-np.log(2) * age / half_life)\n        absolute[half_life] = max(float(np.average(np.abs(normalized), weights=weights) * np.sqrt(np.pi / 2)), 1e-8)\n        root_square[half_life] = max(float(np.sqrt(np.average(normalized ** 2, weights=weights))), 1e-8)\n    return absolute, root_square\n\n\ndef _daily_multiplier(absolute, root_square, asset):\n    reference = absolute[360]\n    values = [np.log(max(estimator[half_life], 1e-9) / reference)\n              for estimator in (absolute, root_square) for half_life in HALF_LIVES]\n    values += [np.log(reference), *[float(asset == name) for name in ASSETS]]\n    weights = _weights()\n    inputs = np.clip((np.asarray(values, dtype=np.float32) - weights[\"center\"]) / weights[\"spread\"], -8, 8)\n    for layer in (0, 2):\n        inputs = weights[f\"{layer}.weight\"] @ inputs + weights[f\"{layer}.bias\"]\n        inputs = inputs / (1 + np.exp(-inputs))\n    output = weights[\"4.weight\"] @ inputs + weights[\"4.bias\"]\n    strength = 1.0 if asset in ASSETS[:5] else COMMODITY_EQUITY_BLEND\n    return float(np.exp(np.clip(output[1], -2, 2))) ** strength\n\n\ndef _volatility_profile(closes):\n    if len(closes) < 2:\n        return np.ones(24)\n    gaps = np.diff(closes.index.as_unit('ns').asi8) / 60e9\n    absolute = np.abs(np.diff(np.log(closes.to_numpy(dtype=float)))) / np.sqrt(gaps)\n    clock = pd.DataFrame({'absolute':absolute,'hour':closes.index[1:].hour,'day':closes.index[1:].date})\n    daily_mean = clock.groupby('day').absolute.transform('mean').clip(lower=1e-9)\n    clock['relative'] = clock.absolute / daily_mean\n    profile = clock.groupby('hour').relative.mean().reindex(range(24),fill_value=1).to_numpy()\n    profile = .25*np.roll(profile,1) + .5*profile + .25*np.roll(profile,-1)\n    profile = np.clip(profile,.25,3)\n    return profile / profile.mean()\n\n\ndef simulate(\n    asset: str,\n    start_time,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n    context_prices=None,\n):\n    if time_increment <= 0 or time_length < 0 or num_simulations < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Positive increment/path count and nonnegative horizon are required\")\n    timestamp = pd.to_datetime(start_time, unit=\"s\", utc=True) if isinstance(start_time, (int, float)) else pd.Timestamp(start_time)\n    timestamp = timestamp.tz_localize(\"UTC\") if timestamp.tzinfo is None else timestamp.tz_convert(\"UTC\")\n    if context_prices is None or \"close\" not in context_prices:\n        raise ValueError(\"A context frame containing close prices is required\")\n    closes = pd.to_numeric(context_prices[\"close\"], errors=\"coerce\").copy()\n    closes.index = pd.to_datetime(closes.index, utc=True)\n    closes = closes.loc[(closes.index > timestamp - pd.Timedelta(days=7)) & (closes.index <= timestamp)]\n    closes = closes.loc[np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0)].sort_index()\n    closes = closes.loc[~closes.index.duplicated(keep=\"last\")]\n    if closes.empty:\n        raise ValueError(\"No finite positive close exists in the seven-day context\")\n    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n    absolute, root_square = _features(closes, timestamp)\n    hourly = time_length <= 3600\n    sigma = absolute[60 if hourly else 360]\n    if not hourly and timestamp >= WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM:\n        sigma *= _daily_multiplier(absolute, root_square, asset)\n    sigma *= np.sqrt(time_increment / 60)\n    seed = int.from_bytes(hashlib.blake2s(f\"{asset}:{timestamp}\".encode(), digest_size=8).digest(), \"little\")\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    steps = time_length // time_increment\n    if not hourly:\n        profile = _volatility_profile(closes)\n        future_times = timestamp + pd.to_timedelta(np.arange(1,steps+1)*time_increment,unit='s')\n        sigma *= 1 + CYCLE_STRENGTH*(profile[future_times.hour]-1)\n    shocks = rng.standard_normal(((num_simulations + 1) // 2, steps))\n    shocks = np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:num_simulations]\n    shocks *= np.sqrt(3 / rng.chisquare(5, size=(num_simulations, 1)))\n    log_paths = np.concatenate([np.zeros((num_simulations, 1)), np.cumsum(shocks * sigma, axis=1)], axis=1)\n    paths = last * np.exp(np.clip(log_paths, -40, 40))\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\n\"\"\"Full-path official backtests and cross-asset validator reward aggregation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport shutil\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\nfrom functools import partial\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom predict import AGENT_DIR, WORKSPACE, backtest, ensure_workspace_cwd, generate, parallel_combined\nfrom research import CRYPTO, EQUITY, WINDOWS, features, generate_variant\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import competition_for, slug_for\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.result import BacktestResult\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.scoring import compute_combined_smoothed_scores\n\n\ndef variant_simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices, variant):\n    feature = features(context_prices, start_time, time_increment)\n    paths = generate_variant(feature, asset, pd.Timestamp(start_time), time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, variant)\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\n\n\ndef evaluate(task):\n    asset, length, window, variant, name = task\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    begin, end = [pd.Timestamp(value, tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime() for value in WINDOWS[window]]\n    increment = 60 if length == 3600 else 300\n    label = f\"{asset}_{length}\"\n    output = AGENT_DIR / \"results\" / name / window\n    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    if (output / f\"{label}_summary.json\").exists():\n        return str(output), label\n    predictions = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / name / window / label / \"predictions\"\n    kwargs = {} if variant == \"model\" else {\"simulator\": partial(variant_simulate, variant=variant)}\n    total = generate(asset, begin, end, time_increment=increment, time_length=length,\n                     num_simulations=1000, predictions_dir=predictions, **kwargs)\n    print(f\"Generated {total} {label} {window}\", flush=True)\n    result = backtest(miner_name=name, asset=asset, time_length=length, time_increment=increment,\n                      n_backtest_days=(end-begin).days, predictions_dir=predictions, eval_end=end)\n    result.prompt_df.to_parquet(output / f\"{label}_prompts.parquet\")\n    result.smoothed_scores.to_parquet(output / f\"{label}_smoothed.parquet\")\n    (output / f\"{label}_summary.json\").write_text(json.dumps(result.summary, indent=2))\n    shutil.rmtree(predictions)\n    return str(output), label\n\n\ndef reward_summary(frame):\n    totals = frame.groupby(\"miner_uid\").reward_weight.sum()\n    latest = frame.loc[frame.updated_at.eq(frame.updated_at.max())].set_index(\"miner_uid\")\n    return {\"reward_rank\": int(totals.rank(ascending=False, method=\"min\").loc[999]),\n            \"final_rank\": int(latest.new_smoothed_score.rank(method=\"min\").loc[999]),\n            \"miners\": int(len(totals)), \"reward_ratio\": float(totals.loc[999] / totals.drop(999).max()),\n            \"reward_rounds\": int(frame.updated_at.nunique()),\n            \"first_round\": str(frame.updated_at.min()), \"last_round\": str(frame.updated_at.max())}\n\n\ndef aggregate(name, window):\n    output = AGENT_DIR / \"results\" / name / window\n    competition_groups = {}\n    for path in sorted(output.glob('*_summary.json')):\n        label = path.name.removesuffix('_summary.json')\n        asset, length = label.rsplit('_', 1)\n        config = competition_for(asset, int(length))\n        result = BacktestResult(name, pd.read_parquet(output / f'{label}_prompts.parquet'),\n                                pd.read_parquet(output / f'{label}_smoothed.parquet'), json.loads(path.read_text()))\n        competition_groups.setdefault(slug_for(config), (config, []))[1].append(result)\n    summaries = {}\n    for label, (config, results) in competition_groups.items():\n        combined_path = output / f'{label}_combined.parquet'\n        combined = pd.read_parquet(combined_path) if combined_path.exists() else parallel_combined(results, config)\n        combined.to_parquet(combined_path)\n        summaries[label] = reward_summary(combined)\n        summaries[label]['assets'] = len(results)\n        print(label, summaries[label], flush=True)\n    summaries['score_estimate'] = 100 * sum(min(1, value['reward_ratio']) for value in summaries.values()) / 3\n    (output / 'competition_metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(summaries, indent=2))\n    return summaries\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--name', required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--variant', default='model')\n    parser.add_argument('--windows', default='dev1,dev2')\n    parser.add_argument('--assets', default=','.join(CRYPTO + EQUITY))\n    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=6)\n    parser.add_argument('--aggregate-only', action='store_true')\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    print((AGENT_DIR / 'BUDGET.md').read_text(), flush=True)\n    if not args.aggregate_only:\n        tasks = [(asset, length, window, args.variant, args.name)\n                 for window in args.windows.split(',') for asset in args.assets.split(',')\n                 for length in ([86400, 3600] if asset in CRYPTO else [86400])]\n        with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.workers) as executor:\n            list(executor.map(evaluate, tasks))\n    for window in args.windows.split(','):\n        print(aggregate(args.name, window), flush=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\"\"\"Frozen-data experiments using only the official scorer exposed by predict.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom time import perf_counter\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom predict import AGENT_DIR, CUTOFF, ensure_workspace_cwd, load_context, score_paths\nfrom auxiliary import auxiliary_features\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import slug_for, competition_for\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.preparation import _slice_real_prices, _fill_gaps_from_realized_paths\n\nCRYPTO = [\"BTC\", \"ETH\", \"SOL\", \"XRP\", \"HYPE\"]\nEQUITY = [\"XAU\", \"NVDAX\", \"GOOGLX\", \"TSLAX\", \"AAPLX\", \"WTIOIL\", \"SPCX\", \"SP500\"]\nWINDOWS = {\"dev1\": (\"2026-07-28\", \"2026-08-07\"), \"dev2\": (\"2026-08-08\", \"2026-08-18\"), \"final\": (\"2026-08-18\", \"2026-08-28\")}\n\n\ndef seed_for(asset, start_time):\n    return int.from_bytes(hashlib.blake2s(f\"{asset}:{start_time}\".encode(), digest_size=8).digest(), \"little\")\n\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=8)\ndef learned_weights(kind='neural'):\n    filename = 'score_weights.npz' if kind == 'curve' else 'volatility_weights.npz'\n    if kind.startswith('refit_'):\n        filename = f'{kind}_weights.npz'\n    if kind=='aux':\n        filename='aux_weights.npz'\n    if kind=='weighted':\n        filename='weighted_score_weights.npz'\n    return dict(np.load(AGENT_DIR / filename))\n\n\ndef learned_multiplier(feature, asset, length, kind):\n    from train_vol import feature_vector\n\n    weights = learned_weights(kind)\n    vector=feature_vector(feature,asset)\n    if kind=='aux':\n        vector=np.r_[vector,feature['auxiliary']]\n    inputs = np.clip((vector - weights['center']) / weights['spread'], -8, 8)\n    head = 0 if length == 3600 else 1\n    if kind == 'ridge':\n        return float(np.clip(1 + np.r_[1, inputs] @ weights['ridge'][:,head], 0.2, 4))\n    for layer in [0, 2]:\n        inputs = weights[f'{layer}.weight'] @ inputs + weights[f'{layer}.bias']\n        inputs = inputs / (1 + np.exp(-inputs))\n    output = weights['4.weight'] @ inputs + weights['4.bias']\n    return float(np.exp(np.clip(output[head], -2, 2)))\n\n\ndef features(context, start_time, increment):\n    close = pd.to_numeric(context[\"close\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n    close = close.loc[np.isfinite(close) & (close > 0)]\n    log_prices = np.log(close.to_numpy())\n    minutes = (close.index - pd.Timestamp(start_time)).total_seconds().to_numpy() / 60\n    gaps = np.diff(minutes)\n    returns = np.diff(log_prices)\n    valid = (gaps > 0) & np.isfinite(returns)\n    returns, gaps, age = returns[valid], gaps[valid], -minutes[1:][valid]\n    normalized = returns / np.sqrt(gaps)\n    output = {\"last\": float(close.iloc[-1]), \"starter\": float(np.std(returns)), \"rv\": {}, \"av\": {}, \"range\": {}}\n    log_ranges, range_age = np.array([]), np.array([])\n    if {'high','low'}.issubset(context.columns):\n        high = pd.to_numeric(context['high'],errors='coerce').to_numpy(dtype=float)\n        low = pd.to_numeric(context['low'],errors='coerce').to_numpy(dtype=float)\n        range_valid = np.isfinite(high) & np.isfinite(low) & (low>0) & (high>=low)\n        log_ranges = np.log(high[range_valid]/low[range_valid])\n        range_age = (pd.Timestamp(start_time)-context.index[range_valid]).total_seconds().to_numpy()/60\n    for half_life in [15, 30, 60, 120, 180, 360, 720, 1440, 2880, 10080]:\n        weights = np.exp(-np.log(2) * age / half_life)\n        output[\"rv\"][half_life] = float(np.sqrt(np.average(normalized ** 2, weights=weights)))\n        output[\"av\"][half_life] = float(np.average(np.abs(normalized), weights=weights) * np.sqrt(np.pi / 2))\n        output['range'][half_life] = output['av'][half_life]\n        if len(log_ranges)>20 and np.any(log_ranges>0):\n            range_weights = np.exp(-np.log(2)*range_age/half_life)\n            output['range'][half_life] = float(np.average(log_ranges,weights=range_weights)*np.sqrt(np.pi/8))\n    raw = pd.to_numeric(context[\"close\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n    raw_log = np.log(raw.where(raw > 0))\n    raw_age = (pd.Timestamp(start_time) - raw.index).total_seconds().to_numpy() / 60\n    for lag in [5, 15, 30, 180]:\n        changes = raw_log.diff(lag).to_numpy() / np.sqrt(lag)\n        valid_changes = np.isfinite(changes)\n        output[f\"av{lag}\"] = {}\n        for half_life in [30, 60, 180, 360, 720, 1440, 2880, 10080]:\n            weights = np.exp(-np.log(2) * raw_age[valid_changes] / half_life)\n            output[f\"av{lag}\"][half_life] = float(np.average(np.abs(changes[valid_changes]), weights=weights) * np.sqrt(np.pi / 2))\n    output[\"returns\"] = normalized\n    clock = pd.DataFrame({'absolute':np.abs(normalized),'hour':close.index[1:][valid].hour,\n                          'day':close.index[1:][valid].date})\n    daily_mean = clock.groupby('day').absolute.transform('mean').clip(lower=1e-9)\n    clock['relative'] = clock.absolute / daily_mean\n    profile = clock.groupby('hour').relative.mean().reindex(range(24),fill_value=1).to_numpy()\n    profile = (.25*np.roll(profile,1) + .5*profile + .25*np.roll(profile,-1))\n    profile = np.clip(profile,.25,3)\n    output['cycle'] = profile / profile.mean()\n    sampled = raw_log.iloc[::-max(1,increment//60)].iloc[::-1].diff()\n    output['step_returns']=sampled.replace([np.inf,-np.inf],np.nan).dropna().to_numpy()\n    differences=np.round(np.abs(np.diff(close.to_numpy())),max(0,10-int(np.floor(np.log10(output['last'])))))\n    positive_differences=differences[differences>0]\n    output['tick']=float(positive_differences.min()) if len(positive_differences) else 0.\n    pairs = pd.concat([sampled,sampled.shift(1)],axis=1).dropna()\n    output['correlation'] = float(pairs.corr().iloc[0,1]) if len(pairs)>20 and (pairs.std()>0).all() else 0.\n    output['auxiliary'],output['auxiliary_usable']=auxiliary_features(context,start_time,max(output['av'][360],1e-8),output['av'])\n    return output\n\n\ndef generate_variant(feature, asset, start_time, increment, length, count, variant):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_for(asset, start_time))\n    steps = length // increment\n    parts = variant.split(\":\")\n    weighted_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='weighted' else None\n    tuned_mode=parts[0]=='tuned'\n    atom_mode=parts[0] if parts[0] in ['symboot','hurdle','quantize'] else None\n    atom_parameter=float(parts[1]) if atom_mode else 0.\n    auxiliary_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='aux' else None\n    range_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0] == 'range' else None\n    correlation_parameter = parts[1] if parts[0] == 'corr' else None\n    prior_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0] == 'prior' else 0.\n    refit_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0] == 'refit' else None\n    if parts[0] == 'quick':\n        parts = ['av',parts[1],'1','5']\n    shape_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0] == \"shape\" else None\n    cycle_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0] == \"cycle\" else 0.\n    if prior_strength:\n        cycle_strength = .75\n        parts = ['hybrid','1']\n    if refit_parameters:\n        cycle_strength = .75\n        parts = ['auto','0','1','5'] if length == 3600 else ['ml','refit_'+refit_parameters[0],refit_parameters[1]]\n    if correlation_parameter is not None:\n        cycle_strength = .75\n        parts = ['hybrid','1']\n    if range_parameters:\n        cycle_strength = .75\n        parts = ['hybrid','1']\n    if auxiliary_strength is not None:\n        cycle_strength=.75\n        parts=['auto','0','1','5']\n    if atom_mode:\n        cycle_strength=.75\n        parts=['hybrid','1']\n    if tuned_mode or weighted_strength is not None:\n        cycle_strength=.75\n        parts=['auto','0','1','5']\n    if shape_parameters:\n        cycle_strength = .75\n        parts = [\"hybrid\", \"1\"]\n    if parts[0] == \"cycle\":\n        parts = [\"hybrid\", \"1\"]\n    if parts[0] == \"hybrid\":\n        strength = 1.0 if asset in CRYPTO else float(parts[1])\n        parts = [\"auto\", \"0\", \"1\", \"5\"] if length == 3600 else [\"ml\", \"neural\", str(strength)]\n    schedule = None\n    learned_scale = 1.0\n    if tuned_mode or weighted_strength is not None:\n        incumbent=learned_multiplier(feature,asset,length,'neural')**(.5 if length==3600 else 1.)\n        learned_scale=incumbent\n        if weighted_strength is not None:\n            learned_scale=incumbent**(1-weighted_strength)*learned_multiplier(feature,asset,length,'weighted')**weighted_strength\n    if auxiliary_strength is not None:\n        incumbent=1. if length==3600 else learned_multiplier(feature,asset,length,'neural')\n        learned_scale=incumbent\n        if feature['auxiliary_usable']:\n            learned_scale=incumbent**(1-auxiliary_strength)*learned_multiplier(feature,asset,length,'aux')**auxiliary_strength\n    innovation = parts[0] if parts[0] in [\"iid\", \"sv\", \"boot\"] else None\n    innovation_parameters = parts[1:]\n    if innovation:\n        parts = [\"auto\", \"0\", \"1\"]\n    if parts[0] == \"ml\":\n# The agent is told to commit often, so anything huge and regenerable must be excluded here:\n# a `git add -A` would otherwise commit a multi-GB .venv (torch + CUDA on GPU campaigns) and\n# 1000-path prediction files at ~5.5MB each. Committed weights are the exception — the champion\n# must stay runnable offline, so DO NOT add model artifacts to this list.\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\nminer_outputs/\nmarket_data/\nagent/BUDGET.md\nagent/*.log\nagent/results/**/*_prompts.parquet\nagent/results/**/*_smoothed.parquet\nagent/results/**/*_combined.parquet\nagent/results/volatility_training.npz\nagent/results/training_score_curves.npz\nagent/results/auxiliary_training.npz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
