{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_235","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 25 result\n+\n+All three ridge penalties worsen chronological validation mean-square error versus zero location: baseline 1.82452; penalties 100/1000/10000 give 1.84238/1.84066/1.83205 on 2,208 validation rows (20,215 training rows). The selector correctly exports zero coefficients. Reject before spending on redundant CRPS screens, because every proposed location path would equal the incumbent. Keep zero log drift; no evidence supports a directional adjustment.\n+\n+### Temporal boundary audit and exact-context refit\n+\n+The cached temporal training sequence includes one return at the seven-day left boundary that runtime cannot form from its supplied frame. Three sampled contexts show differences only in the first hourly bin: maximum 0.0167–0.0284, with every later bin exactly equal. This is older-context mismatch, not future leakage; all development predictions already used the exact runtime context. Nonetheless, refit a separately named \"'`temporal_exact` artifact using the runtime feature function for every training row before promotion. Preserve the original artifact/results rather than silently changing their provenance.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/train_temporal.py\n@@\n-import json\n+import argparse\n+import json\n@@\n-from temporal import hourly_observations, normalize_sequence\n+from temporal import context_sequence, hourly_observations, normalize_sequence\n@@\n-def make_asset(asset):\n+def make_asset(task):\n+    asset, exact = task\n@@\n-    hourly = hourly_observations(prices.close)\n-    sequences = [normalize_sequence(hourly, timestamp, np.exp(data['\"'inputs'][index, 16]))\n-                 for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n+    if exact:\n+        sequences = [context_sequence(prices.loc[timestamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7):timestamp], timestamp, np.exp(data['inputs'][index, 16]))\n+                     for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n+    else:\n+        hourly = hourly_observations(prices.close)\n+        sequences = [normalize_sequence(hourly, timestamp, np.exp(data['inputs'][index, 16]))\n+                     for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n@@\n     ensure_workspace_cwd()\n     print((AGENT_DIR / 'BUDGET.md').read_text(), flush=True)\n-    path = AGENT_DIR / 'results' / 'temporal_training.npz'\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument('--exact-context', action='store_true')\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+    name = 'temporal_exact' if args.exact_context else 'temporal'\n+    path = AGENT_DIR / 'results' / f'{name}_training.npz'\n@@\n-            batches = list(executor.map(make_asset, ASSETS))\n+            batches = list(executor.map(make_asset, [(asset,args.exact_context) for asset in ASSETS]))\n@@\n-    np.savez(AGENT_DIR / 'temporal_weights.npz', center=previous['center'], spread=previous['spread'], **best_state)\n+    np.savez(AGENT_DIR / f'{name}_weights.npz', center=previous['center'], spread=previous['spread'], **best_state)\n@@\n-               'training_rows': int(training.sum()), 'validation_rows': int((~training).sum())}\n-    (AGENT_DIR / 'temporal_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics, indent=2))\n+               'training_rows': int(training.sum()), 'validation_rows': int((~training).sum()), 'exact_context': args.exact_context}\n+    (AGENT_DIR / f'{name}_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics, indent=2))\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/temporal.py\n@@\n-@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n-def temporal_weights():\n-    return dict(np.load(Path(__file__).with_name('temporal_weights.npz')))\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=2)\n+def temporal_weights(kind='temporal'):\n+    return dict(np.load(Path(__file__).with_name(f'{kind}_weights.npz')))\n@@\n-def temporal_residual(sequence, static):\n-    weights = temporal_weights()\n+def temporal_residual(sequence, static, kind='temporal'):\n+    weights = temporal_weights(kind)\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['temporal','combined'] else None\n+    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['temporal','temporal_exact','combined'] else None\n+    temporal_kind='temporal_exact' if parts[0]=='temporal_exact' else 'temporal'\n@@\n-            residual = temporal_residual(feature['temporal'],feature_vector(feature,asset))\n+            residual = temporal_residual(feature['temporal'],feature_vector(feature,asset),temporal_kind)\n*** Update File: /workspace/.gitignore\n@@\n agent/results/temporal_training.npz\n+agent/results/temporal_exact_training.npz\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/train_temporal.py --exact-context > agent/train_temporal_exact.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_236","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -6 agent/temporal_daily_dense.log; tail -8 agent/hourly_refinements_dense.log; cat agent/BUDGET.md; sed -n '40,110p' agent/report.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_236","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -6 agent/temporal_daily_dense.log; tail -8 agent/hourly_refinements_dense.log; cat agent/BUDGET.md; sed -n '40,110p' agent/report.md\"","aggregated_output":"WTIOIL filled 98/98 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 GOOGLX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\nSPCX filled 50/50 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 TSLAX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\nSP500 filled 60/60 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 AAPLX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\nHYPE filled 6/6 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev1 XRP 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\ndev2 BTC 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\ndev1 SOL 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\ndev1 HYPE 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\nHYPE filled 14/14 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev1 ETH 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\ndev1 BTC 3600: 1440 prompts, 5 variants\n# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 28.41 / 100.00 USD (28%)\n- Time   : 1.8 h elapsed, 16.2 h remaining (10%)\n- Phase  : normal\n\n| Experiment | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Recent RMS versus absolute-return volatility | Robust recent scale wins consistently; the seven-day starter adapts too slowly. |\n| One-hour versus six-hour memory | Hourly and daily formats need different memories. A short daily memory overreacts. |\n| Gaussian versus Student path mixtures | A modest heavy-tailed mixture improves calibration; extreme dispersion does not. |\n| Five-/15-/30-minute calibration returns | No universal improvement over the minute-based robust estimator. |\n| Hand-designed volatility reversion | Small, inconsistent gains; not retained. |\n| Pooled neural forecasting | Material daily gains, but the full hourly correction does not improve mean CRPS. |\n| IID tails, stochastic volatility, empirical bootstrap | The tested more complicated dynamics do not beat the simple mixture consistently. |\n| Official-score-curve fine-tuning | 95,750 official training scores produce only a tiny interpolation-loss gain that does not transfer consistently. |\n| Positive local periodic profile | Improves both daily competitions across both development regimes. |\n| Moment-matched tail grids | No consistent material improvement over the incumbent mixture. |\n| Historical profile prior and alternative short memories | Added complexity has negligible or mixed gains. |\n| Recency-weighted neural refitting | Small, consistent CRPS gains; retained for reward-based confirmation, not automatically adopted. |\n| Serial return correlation | Estimated correlation is essentially a null result; fixed correlations overfit regimes. |\n| Direct high/low range substitution | Does not transfer consistently; a fixed diffusion-based range calibration is inadequate. |\n\nTwo ongoing investigations deserve attention. First, dense hourly reward replays suggest that small mean-CRPS differences can produce large changes in emissions. Second, the snapshot contains nonmissing, internally coherent OHLCV data despite its close-only description. An auxiliary-feature model and discrete-return models are being tested; neither is yet accepted.\n\nAn implementation failure is included rather than hidden: the first training-label build treated microsecond timestamps as nanoseconds, inflating scale ratios by the square root of 1000. Target-distribution checks caught it before any learned candidate was scored. Those artifacts were discarded, timestamp units were made explicit, and training was rebuilt.\n\n## Results\n\nFull 1000-path starter replays produce Score estimates **0.32375** and **0.42456** on the two development windows.\n\nThe full incumbent replay has completed the first window:\n\n| Competition | Starter reward rank | Incumbent reward rank | Incumbent reward / best field reward |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| COM_EQU_24H | 239 / 257 | 174 / 257 | 0.000498 |\n| CRYPTO_1H | 216 / 257 | 136 / 257 | 0.368394 |\n| CRYPTO_24H | 236 / 257 | 118 / 257 | 0.135626 |\n\nThis corresponds to a Score estimate of **16.8173**, versus 0.32375 for the starter. It is substantial progress, but not field leadership. Commodity/equity emissions remain particularly weak. The second incumbent replay, hourly finalist selection, and the reserved final validation are not yet complete; their results must not be inferred from this table.\n\nThese are historical reward estimates, not the campaign's eventual post-cutoff Score. Sampled terminal-rank diagnostics and reward-round-thinned screens are explicitly labeled and are not substituted for full final replay.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- The effective validation sample consists of market days and regimes, not thousands of independent prompt observations. Overlapping horizons create dependence.\n- Many hypotheses are screened on the same development windows. The reserved final window remains necessary, and small grid gains may be selection noise.\n- The pinned configuration uses ten-day daily and five-day hourly smoothing windows. Default backtester warmup trimming therefore gives different effective reward intervals; reports must state those intervals rather than repeat the campaign prose's 24-hour description.\n- The official backtester may replace NaN-holed realized paths with cached validator truth. This behavior is preserved, not silently altered.\n- A context with no finite positive close cannot supply the required starting price; the model raises a clear error instead of inventing one.\n- The frozen-data interface does not provide contemporaneous cross-asset information or external news. Additional information used by live miners may not be reproducible here.\n- A bounded historical score-only API probe returned out-of-request timestamps and was rejected before any score analysis or storage. Evaluation remains strictly offline, with a fail-closed environment check.\n\n## What we would do with more budget\n\nThe campaign still has budget and is continuing. Priorities are to finish emission-sensitive hourly selection, evaluate optional candle/activity information and discrete return distributions, investigate whether a learned lead-time volatility profile adds value, and consider strictly chronological field-aware calibration. Any additional fitted checkpoint must be available before the predictions it evaluates. Final nomination requires a frozen model, a full 1000-path field replay, interface checks, and committed artifacts—not an attractive development-only CRPS table.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_224","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 24 — scale/shape interaction (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the temporal residual changes mean forecast scale while the lead-time network redistributes scale over the day, so their gains may be complementary rather than redundant.\n+- Change: at 1000 paths, compare tuned, half/full temporal residual, and each temporal strength combined with half lead shape, on every archived daily prompt in both development windows. Hourly is handled separately because lead shape is inactive there.\n+- Result: pending. The standalone temporal screen improves all six competition/window cells at half strength (COM_EQU 0.99792/0.99387, hourly 0.99965/0.99959, daily crypto 0.99970/0.99808). Full temporal improves equities further but is less stable elsewhere. Its pre-development likelihood improves 1.01930→1.00675, selected at epoch 24; NumPy/Torch outputs agree within 2e-6 and future-row invariance passes.\n+- Verdict: select a combined candidate only if dense official CRPS and rewards improve both windows; otherwise keep the simpler component.\n+- Lesson: pending; held-out likelihood and actual rewards remain distinct diagnostics.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    lead_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n-    sampler=parts[1] if parts[0]=='sampler' else None\n+    lead_strength=float(parts[2]) if parts[0]=='combined' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n+    sampler=parts[3] if parts[0]=='combined' and len(parts)>3 else parts[1] if parts[0]=='sampler' else None\n@@\n-    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='temporal' else None\n+    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['temporal','combined'] else None\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/research.py --name temporal_daily_dense --variants tuned,temporal:0.5,temporal:1,combined:0.5:0.5,combined:1:0.5 --format low --paths 1000 --stride-low 1 --workers 4 > agent/temporal_daily_dense.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_237","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/report.md\n@@\n-Daily forecasts additionally use a small pooled neural volatility model. Its 30 inputs summarize eight absolute-return and eight RMS scales, their ratios, the absolute volatility level, and asset identity. A 48/32-unit network predicts a multiplicative volatility correction. Training uses 23,457 contexts before July 1, with 2,508 July 1–25 contexts for chronological model selection. All labels end before July 26. Serving uses exported NumPy weights, not a GPU or a network call.\n+Both formats additionally use a small pooled neural volatility model, at full strength daily and half strength hourly. Its 30 inputs summarize eight absolute-return and eight RMS scales, their ratios, the absolute volatility level, and asset identity. A 48/32-unit network predicts a multiplicative volatility correction. Training uses 23,457 contexts before July 1, with 2,508 July 1–25 contexts for chronological model selection. All labels end before July 26. Serving uses exported NumPy weights, not a GPU or a network call.\n@@\n A positive, smoothed hourly volatility profile is estimated from the supplied past seven days and shrunk 25% toward a flat curve. This is **not a market-session model**: there are no opening/closing times, exchange calendars, weekend switches, or zero-volatility hours. The empirical finding is simply that continuous trading does not imply constant variance throughout a day.\n+\n+A second small network predicts volatility in five future daily buckets: minutes 0–60, 60–180, 180–360, 360–720 and 720–1440. Its output is normalized to unit mean and applied at half strength, redistributing uncertainty over lead time without changing average scale. This component passes full official reward replay in both development windows.\n@@\n-Two ongoing investigations deserve attention. First, dense hourly reward replays suggest that small mean-CRPS differences can produce large changes in emissions. Second, the snapshot contains nonmissing, internally coherent OHLCV data despite its close-only description. An auxiliary-feature model and discrete-return models are being tested; neither is yet accepted.\n+Dense hourly reward replays confirm that small mean-CRPS differences can produce large changes in emissions. The auxiliary OHLCV network and empirical/discrete-return variants do not pass the consistency gate. Correcting the score-curve objective to raw, asset-weighted CRPS also fails to produce a consistent fitted gain; it remains a methodological correction, not a successful model improvement. Five-minute supervised targets and conditional directional ridge forecasts are rejected. Direct scrambled Sobol sampling has small, mostly seed-robust gains at 1000 paths and remains under reward confirmation. A temporal convolutional residual improves chronological likelihood and development CRPS, but is not yet promoted; an exact-context refit corrects a one-return mismatch in its oldest training bin.\n@@\n-The full incumbent replay has completed the first window:\n+Full official reward replay supports the current hourly-plus-lead-shaped incumbent:\n@@\n-| Competition | Starter reward rank | Incumbent reward rank | Incumbent reward / best field reward |\n-|---|---:|---:|---:|\n-| COM_EQU_24H | 239 / 257 | 174 / 257 | 0.000498 |\n-| CRYPTO_1H | 216 / 257 | 136 / 257 | 0.368394 |\n-| CRYPTO_24H | 236 / 257 | 118 / 257 | 0.135626 |\n+| Window | Competition | Starter reward rank | Incumbent reward rank | Incumbent reward / best field reward |\n+|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n+| dev1 | COM_EQU_24H | 239 / 257 | 174 / 257 | 0.000785 |\n+| dev1 | CRYPTO_1H | 216 / 257 | 87 / 257 | 0.629991 |\n+| dev1 | CRYPTO_24H | 236 / 257 | 97 / 257 | 0.151344 |\n+| dev2 | COM_EQU_24H | 248 / 257 | 230 / 257 | 0.000442 |\n+| dev2 | CRYPTO_1H | 227 / 257 | 135 / 257 | 0.704092 |\n+| dev2 | CRYPTO_24H | 257 / 257 | 227 / 257 | 0.058647 |\n@@\n-This corresponds to a Score estimate of **16.8173**, versus 0.32375 for the starter. It is substantial progress, but not field leadership. Commodity/equity emissions remain particularly weak. The second incumbent replay, hourly finalist selection, and the reserved final validation are not yet complete; their results must not be inferred from this table.\n+These correspond to development Score estimates **26.071** and **25.439**, versus 0.32375 and 0.42456 for the starter. It is substantial progress, but not field leadership. Commodity/equity emissions remain particularly weak. Each row uses all official reward rounds for its selected candidate; hourly has 1,624/1,847 post-warmup rounds, daily crypto 1,015/1,044, and COM_EQU 1,499/1,474. Production and research paths match numerically on representative assets and both formats. The reserved final validation remains untouched.\n@@\n-The campaign still has budget and is continuing. Priorities are to finish emission-sensitive hourly selection, evaluate optional candle/activity information and discrete return distributions, investigate whether a learned lead-time volatility profile adds value, and consider strictly chronological field-aware calibration. Any additional fitted checkpoint must be available before the predictions it evaluates. Final nomination requires a frozen model, a full 1000-path field replay, interface checks, and committed artifacts—not an attractive development-only CRPS table.\n+The campaign still has budget and is continuing. Priorities are to confirm temporal/lead interactions, finish finite-ensemble and hourly emission-sensitive selection, and stress-test chronological calibration. Any additional fitted checkpoint must be available before the predictions it evaluates. Final nomination requires a frozen model, a full 1000-path field replay with explicit warmup handling, interface checks, and committed artifacts—not an attractive development-only CRPS table.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run python -m compileall -q agent\ngit add .gitignore agent/*.py agent/*.md agent/*weights.npz agent/*weights.json agent/results/*.parquet agent/results/*ranks.json && git -c user.name='Campaign Research Agent' -c user.email='campaign-agent@localhost' commit -m 'Promote confirmed hourly and lead models; audit temporal and location extensions'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
