{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_235","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 25 result\n+\n+All three ridge penalties worsen chronological validation mean-square error versus zero location: baseline 1.82452; penalties 100/1000/10000 give 1.84238/1.84066/1.83205 on 2,208 validation rows (20,215 training rows). The selector correctly exports zero coefficients. Reject before spending on redundant CRPS screens, because every proposed location path would equal the incumbent. Keep zero log drift; no evidence supports a directional adjustment.\n+\n+### Temporal boundary audit and exact-context refit\n+\n+The cached temporal training sequence includes one return at the seven-day left boundary that runtime cannot form from its supplied frame. Three sampled contexts show differences only in the first hourly bin: maximum 0.0167–0.0284, with every later bin exactly equal. This is older-context mismatch, not future leakage; all development predictions already used the exact runtime context. Nonetheless, refit a separately named \"'`temporal_exact` artifact using the runtime feature function for every training row before promotion. Preserve the original artifact/results rather than silently changing their provenance.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/train_temporal.py\n@@\n-import json\n+import argparse\n+import json\n@@\n-from temporal import hourly_observations, normalize_sequence\n+from temporal import context_sequence, hourly_observations, normalize_sequence\n@@\n-def make_asset(asset):\n+def make_asset(task):\n+    asset, exact = task\n@@\n-    hourly = hourly_observations(prices.close)\n-    sequences = [normalize_sequence(hourly, timestamp, np.exp(data['\"'inputs'][index, 16]))\n-                 for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n+    if exact:\n+        sequences = [context_sequence(prices.loc[timestamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7):timestamp], timestamp, np.exp(data['inputs'][index, 16]))\n+                     for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n+    else:\n+        hourly = hourly_observations(prices.close)\n+        sequences = [normalize_sequence(hourly, timestamp, np.exp(data['inputs'][index, 16]))\n+                     for timestamp, index in zip(timestamps, indices)]\n@@\n     ensure_workspace_cwd()\n     print((AGENT_DIR / 'BUDGET.md').read_text(), flush=True)\n-    path = AGENT_DIR / 'results' / 'temporal_training.npz'\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument('--exact-context', action='store_true')\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+    name = 'temporal_exact' if args.exact_context else 'temporal'\n+    path = AGENT_DIR / 'results' / f'{name}_training.npz'\n@@\n-            batches = list(executor.map(make_asset, ASSETS))\n+            batches = list(executor.map(make_asset, [(asset,args.exact_context) for asset in ASSETS]))\n@@\n-    np.savez(AGENT_DIR / 'temporal_weights.npz', center=previous['center'], spread=previous['spread'], **best_state)\n+    np.savez(AGENT_DIR / f'{name}_weights.npz', center=previous['center'], spread=previous['spread'], **best_state)\n@@\n-               'training_rows': int(training.sum()), 'validation_rows': int((~training).sum())}\n-    (AGENT_DIR / 'temporal_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics, indent=2))\n+               'training_rows': int(training.sum()), 'validation_rows': int((~training).sum()), 'exact_context': args.exact_context}\n+    (AGENT_DIR / f'{name}_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics, indent=2))\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/temporal.py\n@@\n-@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n-def temporal_weights():\n-    return dict(np.load(Path(__file__).with_name('temporal_weights.npz')))\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=2)\n+def temporal_weights(kind='temporal'):\n+    return dict(np.load(Path(__file__).with_name(f'{kind}_weights.npz')))\n@@\n-def temporal_residual(sequence, static):\n-    weights = temporal_weights()\n+def temporal_residual(sequence, static, kind='temporal'):\n+    weights = temporal_weights(kind)\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['temporal','combined'] else None\n+    temporal_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['temporal','temporal_exact','combined'] else None\n+    temporal_kind='temporal_exact' if parts[0]=='temporal_exact' else 'temporal'\n@@\n-            residual = temporal_residual(feature['temporal'],feature_vector(feature,asset))\n+            residual = temporal_residual(feature['temporal'],feature_vector(feature,asset),temporal_kind)\n*** Update File: /workspace/.gitignore\n@@\n agent/results/temporal_training.npz\n+agent/results/temporal_exact_training.npz\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/train_temporal.py --exact-context > agent/train_temporal_exact.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_242","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 26 — smooth data-fitted periodic scale (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: continuously traded markets can have smooth activity cycles even without sessions or closures. Past-week clock shape does not explicitly forecast how average future volatility depends on the current phase of those cycles.\n+- Change: fit a strongly regularized positive scale residual from daily/weekly sine and cosine harmonics, shared and interacted with asset identity. Fit only the pre-July-1 rows and select regularization on July 1–25; use the confirmed half-hourly/full-daily neural baseline. Bound log corrections at +/-0.5 and test half/full strengths. There are no exchange calendars, market-hour gates, weekend exclusions, or zero-volatility bins.\n+- Result: pending chronological likelihood and official development CRPS against the lead-shaped incumbent.\n+- Verdict: require consistent gains; reject rather than invent a trading-session explanation if the data do not support this periodic predictor.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/periodic.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Smooth positive scale corrections, without market-session assumptions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+from functools import lru_cache\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+\n+def periodic_design(timestamps, asset_indices, asset_count=13):\n+    timestamps = pd.DatetimeIndex(timestamps)\n+    day = (timestamps.hour + timestamps.minute / 60 + timestamps.second / 3600) / 24\n+    week = (timestamps.dayofweek + day) / 7\n+    harmonic = np.column_stack([function(2*np.pi*frequency*phase)\n+                               for phase in [day,week] for frequency in [1,2] for function in [np.sin,np.cos]])\n+    indicator = np.eye(asset_count)[asset_indices]\n+    interactions = (harmonic[:, :, None] * indicator[:, None, :]).reshape(len(timestamps), -1)\n+    return np.column_stack([harmonic,interactions])\n+\n+\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n+def periodic_weights():\n+    return dict(np.load(Path(__file__).with_name('periodic_weights.npz')))\n+\n+\n+def periodic_multiplier(asset_index, timestamp, length):\n+    design = periodic_design(pd.DatetimeIndex([timestamp]),np.array([asset_index]))\n+    output = design @ periodic_weights()['coefficients']\n+    return float(np.exp(np.clip(output[0,0 if length==3600 else 1],-.5,.5)))\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/fit_periodic.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Chronological harmonic likelihood fitting around the tuned baseline.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import json\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+from scipy.optimize import minimize\n+\n+from periodic import periodic_design\n+from predict import AGENT_DIR, ensure_workspace_cwd\n+\n+ensure_workspace_cwd()\n+print((AGENT_DIR / 'BUDGET.md').read_text(),flush=True)\n+data = np.load(AGENT_DIR / 'results' / 'volatility_training.npz')\n+previous = dict(np.load(AGENT_DIR / 'volatility_weights.npz'))\n+inputs = data['inputs']\n+timestamps = pd.to_datetime(data['timestamps'],utc=True)\n+training = timestamps < pd.Timestamp('2026-07-01',tz='UTC')\n+design = periodic_design(timestamps,np.argmax(inputs[:,-13:],axis=1))\n+hidden = np.clip((inputs-previous['center'])/previous['spread'],-8,8)\n+for layer in [0,2]:\n+    hidden = hidden @ previous[f'{layer}.weight'].T + previous[f'{layer}.bias']\n+    hidden = hidden/(1+np.exp(-hidden))\n+baseline = np.clip(hidden @ previous['4.weight'].T+previous['4.bias'],-2,2)\n+baseline[:,0] *= .5\n+targets = np.clip(data['targets'],.02,20)\n+ratio = targets/np.exp(baseline)\n+initial = float(np.mean(ratio[~training]+baseline[~training]))\n+best, best_penalty = initial, None\n+best_coefficients = np.zeros((design.shape[1],2))\n+diagnostics = {}\n+train_design, train_ratio = design[training],ratio[training]\n+for penalty in [.001,.01,.1]:\n+    def objective(flattened):\n+        coefficients = flattened.reshape(design.shape[1],2)\n+        raw = train_design @ coefficients\n+        correction = np.clip(raw,-.5,.5)\n+        scaled = train_ratio*np.exp(-correction)\n+        loss = np.mean(scaled+correction)+penalty*np.sum(coefficients**2)\n+        gradient = train_design.T @ ((1-scaled)*(np.abs(raw)<.5))/scaled.size+2*penalty*coefficients\n+        return float(loss),gradient.ravel()\n+\n+    fitted = minimize(objective,np.zeros(design.shape[1]*2),method='L-BFGS-B',jac=True,\n+                      options={'maxiter':200,'ftol':1e-10})\n+    coefficients = fitted.x.reshape(design.shape[1],2)\n+    correction = np.clip(design[~training] @ coefficients,-.5,.5)\n+    loss = float(np.mean(ratio[~training]*np.exp(-correction)+baseline[~training]+correction))\n+    diagnostics[str(penalty)] = {'validation_loss':loss,'optimizer_success':bool(fitted.success),'iterations':int(fitted.nit)}\n+    if loss<best:\n+        best,best_penalty,best_coefficients = loss,penalty,coefficients\n+    print(penalty,diagnostics[str(penalty)],flush=True)\n+np.savez(AGENT_DIR / 'periodic_weights.npz',coefficients=best_coefficients)\n+metrics = {'initial_validation_loss':initial,'best_validation_loss':best,'penalty':best_penalty,\n+           'diagnostics':diagnostics,'target_cutoff':'2026-07-26','validation_start':'2026-07-01',\n+           'interpretation':'Smooth bounded positive scale only; no session gates or closures.'}\n+(AGENT_DIR / 'periodic_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2))\n+print(metrics,flush=True)\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0]=='location' else float(parts[2]) if parts[0]=='combined' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n+    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0] in ['location','periodic'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0]=='combined' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n@@\n     location_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='location' else None\n+    periodic_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='periodic' else None\n@@\n         learned_scale=incumbent\n+        if periodic_strength is not None:\n+            from periodic import periodic_multiplier\n+\n+            learned_scale *= periodic_multiplier((CRYPTO+EQUITY).index(asset),start_time,length)**periodic_strength\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 uv run agent/fit_periodic.py > agent/fit_periodic.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
