crypto-1h         1.0                     1.000066                   1.000309                1.000086              1.000332\n       crypto-24h        1.0                     1.000153                   1.000565                1.000150              1.000552\ndev2   com-equ-24h       1.0                     1.000646                   1.001330                1.000572              1.001164\n       crypto-1h         1.0                     1.000384                   1.000568                1.000368              1.000553\n       crypto-24h        1.0                     1.000988                   1.002254                1.000996              1.002264\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_258","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '210,240p' agent/journal.md; rg -n 'Iteration 9 result|cycle|0.75|0.5/1' agent/journal.md | tail -16; ls agent/results/*.parquet | sed -n '1,50p'; cat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -5 agent/hourly_refinements_ranks.log; tail -5 agent/temporal_exact_daily_ranks.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_258","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '210,240p' agent/journal.md; rg -n 'Iteration 9 result|cycle|0.75|0.5/1' agent/journal.md | tail -16; ls agent/results/*.parquet | sed -n '1,50p'; cat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -5 agent/hourly_refinements_ranks.log; tail -5 agent/temporal_exact_daily_ranks.log\"","aggregated_output":"\n### Field-relative reality check\n\nThe sampled official final-round replay favors full daily neural correction over half-strength COM_EQU correction in both windows, so use full correction provisionally. However, low CRPS improvements do NOT imply field competitiveness: daily crypto sampled reward ratios are only 0.0250/0.0070 and COM_EQU about 1.2e-6/9.9e-7. Hourly ratios are 0.206/0.582. These are sampled end-round diagnostics, not the final cumulative-emission Score. The remaining daily gap is material, so early nomination is not justified. Continue research.\n\n## Iteration 9 — empirical periodic volatility, not sessions (preregistered)\n\n- Hypothesis: a flat daily variance forecast misses repeating information-flow patterns even on a venue that trades continuously. A weak periodic profile estimated exclusively from the supplied past seven days may improve daily paths.\n- Change: normalize past absolute returns within each observed calendar day, estimate a smoothed 24-hour profile, and shrink toward a flat positive curve. Test strengths 0.25/0.5/0.75/1 against the full daily-neural incumbent. This has NO exchange calendar, open/close boundary, weekend switch, or zero-volatility session. Every hour remains active; this experiment tests whether a periodic pattern exists rather than assuming one.\n- Result: pending. Price NaNs remain dropped, never interpolated; smoothing applies only to estimated volatility parameters.\n- Verdict: retain only if both development windows show consistent official CRPS gains; otherwise discard the periodic hypothesis.\n- Lesson: pending.\n\n### Iteration 9 result\n\nThe empirical positive volatility profile clears the gate. Relative to the daily-neural incumbent, strength 0.75 gives COM_EQU_24H 0.98653/0.98038 and daily crypto 0.99567/0.99463; strength 1 gives 0.98496/0.97800 and 0.99577/0.99467. Hourly is unchanged. Thus continuous trading does not imply a flat variance clock in this snapshot. Prefer the slightly shrunk 0.75 profile provisionally and validate full field emissions at 1000 paths; do not reinterpret this as exchange-session closures.\n\n### Iteration 8 training result\n\nComputed 95,750 official CRPS values at 128 paths over 6,081 pre-field contexts, with 9,575 valid context/horizon pairs. Score-aware fine-tuning improves the chronological interpolated validation ratio only from 0.992970 to 0.992561, peaking at epoch 5; longer fitting overfits. The new model is now undergoing fresh official development-window CRPS screening. This tiny training gain alone does not justify deployment.\n\n### Iteration 8 held-out result\n\nReject score-aware fine-tuning: full correction relative to the likelihood-trained hybrid gives COM_EQU_24H 1.00084/0.99619, hourly 1.00094/1.00123, and daily crypto 0.99995/0.99953. The small training-objective gain does not transfer consistently, and hourly still regresses. Keep the likelihood-trained daily model and classical hourly model.\n\n## Iteration 10 — moment-matched tail calibration (preregistered)\n\n- Hypothesis: previous shape comparisons fixed RMS, which changes expected absolute movement across Student degrees of freedom. Matching the absolute first moment may expose a better shape/scale pair, especially for peaked commodity/equity returns.\n- Change: hold the neural-plus-0.75-cycle forecaster fixed; compare Student df 3/5/8 and Gaussian shapes at expected absolute movements 0.8/0.9/1.0/1.1 times the predicted absolute scale. The Student normalizing factor is analytic; every forecast CRPS is still computed only by the official scorer.\n- Result: pending. Screening at 256 paths precedes 1000-path confirmation and coefficient-weighted field selection.\n- Verdict: retain only consistent cross-window gains, not an isolated grid winner.\n13:- Hypothesis: continuously traded markets can have smooth activity cycles even without sessions or closures. Past-week clock shape does not explicitly forecast how average future volatility depends on the current phase of those cycles.\n37:At 1000 paths and every official reward round, half lead shape improves daily crypto reward ratios 0.135626→0.151344 (rank 118→97) and 0.037376→0.058647 (rank 230→227), and COM_EQU 0.000498→0.000785 (rank unchanged at 174) and 0.000156→0.000442 (rank 231→230). There are 1,499/1,474 equity rounds and 1,015/1,044 daily-crypto rounds in dev1/dev2. Promote half lead shape with its pre-July-26 weights. Combined with the confirmed hourly correction, development Score estimates become 26.071 and 25.439. The remaining daily reward gap is still large, so continue the campaign.\n47:- Result: pending. The standalone temporal screen improves all six competition/window cells at half strength (COM_EQU 0.99792/0.99387, hourly 0.99965/0.99959, daily crypto 0.99970/0.99808). Full temporal improves equities further but is less stable elsewhere. Its pre-development likelihood improves 1.01930→1.00675, selected at epoch 24; NumPy/Torch outputs agree within 2e-6 and future-row invariance passes.\n105:Correct raw-score weighting improves the held-out curve objective only slightly, from 0.795870 to 0.795527 (epoch 28). Half-strength official CRPS ratios to `tuned` are COM_EQU 0.99895/1.00073, hourly 1.00045/1.00010, daily crypto 0.99967/1.00111. Full-strength regresses further in dev2. Sparse end-round official reward checks confirm the lack of consistency: daily-crypto ratios change 0.07663→0.09110 in dev1 but 0.02316→0.01649 in dev2; hourly changes 0.86748→0.72852 and 0.53715→0.47545. These single-round, reduced-path numbers are screening diagnostics, not campaign Score estimates. Discard the fitted correction, retain the objective-rule correction as an important methodological lesson.\n218:- Change: normalize past absolute returns within each observed calendar day, estimate a smoothed 24-hour profile, and shrink toward a flat positive curve. Test strengths 0.25/0.5/0.75/1 against the full daily-neural incumbent. This has NO exchange calendar, open/close boundary, weekend switch, or zero-volatility session. Every hour remains active; this experiment tests whether a periodic pattern exists rather than assuming one.\n223:### Iteration 9 result\n225:The empirical positive volatility profile clears the gate. Relative to the daily-neural incumbent, strength 0.75 gives COM_EQU_24H 0.98653/0.98038 and daily crypto 0.99567/0.99463; strength 1 gives 0.98496/0.97800 and 0.99577/0.99467. Hourly is unchanged. Thus continuous trading does not imply a flat variance clock in this snapshot. Prefer the slightly shrunk 0.75 profile provisionally and validate full field emissions at 1000 paths; do not reinterpret this as exchange-session closures.\n238:- Change: hold the neural-plus-0.75-cycle forecaster fixed; compare Student df 3/5/8 and Gaussian shapes at expected absolute movements 0.8/0.9/1.0/1.1 times the predicted absolute scale. The Student normalizing factor is analytic; every forecast CRPS is still computed only by the official scorer.\n250:- Change: fit positive per-asset hourly profiles from April 1 (or first trade) through July 26, using the same within-day normalization and circular smoothing. Blend 25/50/75/100% historical prior into the local profile; keep total cycle strength 0.75. Separately check 15/30/60/120-minute robust half-lives for hourly forecasts, changing nothing else.\n262:- Change: initialize from the likelihood model, make 40 fixed-epoch passes over all pre-July-26 labels, and compare uniform versus 60/120-day exponential recency weights. No development or final-window labels enter the fit. Daily correction remains full strength with the 0.75 local profile; hourly stays classical. Compare optional half-strength shrinkage only if full corrections regress.\n277:Recency refitting gives small but directionally consistent gains. The 60-day weighted refit gives COM_EQU_24H 0.99942/0.99812 and CRYPTO_24H 0.99926/0.99901 versus the current neural-cycle incumbent. These are below the original 0.5% CRPS screen threshold, so do not replace the weights yet. Because emissions are nonlinear, retain this as a candidate for coefficient-weighted reward confirmation rather than treating the threshold as proof of no utility.\n282:- Change: preserve the full neural-plus-local-cycle incumbent and df5 marginal mixture; generate stationary AR(1) Gaussian innovations at correlations -0.2/-0.1/+0.1/+0.2, plus a half-shrunk correlation estimated from valid adjacent context returns at the served step size. No price interpolation, drift signal, or future information is used.\n337:The neural-plus-0.75-local-cycle model reaches official cumulative Score estimate 16.8173 on dev1, versus 0.32375 for the starter. Reward ranks / ratios to the field's best: COM_EQU_24H 174/257 and 0.0004981; CRYPTO_1H 136/257 and 0.368394; CRYPTO_24H 118/257 and 0.135626. This is substantial progress but not field leadership, especially for commodities/equities. Dev2 full replay is still running.\nagent/results/auxiliary_screen.parquet\nagent/results/clock_prior_screen.parquet\nagent/results/correlation_screen.parquet\nagent/results/cycle_screen.parquet\nagent/results/dense_confirmation.parquet\nagent/results/discrete_screen.parquet\nagent/results/dynamics_screen.parquet\nagent/results/ensemble_screen.parquet\nagent/results/fiveminute_screen.parquet\nagent/results/half_life_screen.parquet\nagent/results/hourly_emission_screen.parquet\nagent/results/hourly_memory_screen.parquet\nagent/results/hourly_refinements_dense.parquet\nagent/results/lead_dense.parquet\nagent/results/lead_screen.parquet\nagent/results/learned_screen.parquet\nagent/results/matched_shape_screen.parquet\nagent/results/periodic_screen.parquet\nagent/results/range_screen.parquet\nagent/results/refit_screen.parquet\nagent/results/reversion_screen.parquet\nagent/results/sampler_screen.parquet\nagent/results/sampler_seeds.parquet\nagent/results/sampling_screen.parquet\nagent/results/scale_mixture_screen.parquet\nagent/results/score_fit_screen.parquet\nagent/results/temporal_daily_dense.parquet\nagent/results/temporal_exact_daily_dense.parquet\nagent/results/temporal_screen.parquet\nagent/results/uncertainty_screen.parquet\nagent/results/volatility_screen.parquet\nagent/results/weighted_score_screen.parquet\n# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 32.15 / 100.00 USD (32%)\n- Time   : 2.0 h elapsed, 16.0 h remaining (11%)\n- Phase  : normal\ndev1/ensemble:1/crypto-1h {'reward_rank': 86, 'final_rank': 140, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.630320734676363, 'reward_rounds': 235, 'first_round': '2026-08-02 00:04:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 23:50:00+00:00'}\ndev1/sampler:sobol/crypto-1h {'reward_rank': 76, 'final_rank': 140, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.6700914974994727, 'reward_rounds': 235, 'first_round': '2026-08-02 00:04:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 23:50:00+00:00'}\ndev1/temporal:0.5/crypto-1h {'reward_rank': 32, 'final_rank': 125, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.7577416309516403, 'reward_rounds': 235, 'first_round': '2026-08-02 00:04:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 23:50:00+00:00'}\ndev1/combined_exact:1:0.5/crypto-24h {'reward_rank': 144, 'final_rank': 130, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.1277925246554584, 'reward_rounds': 87, 'first_round': '2026-07-28 00:13:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 13:00:00+00:00'}\ndev1/lead:0.5/com-equ-24h {'reward_rank': 174, 'final_rank': 171, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.0008349378267724609, 'reward_rounds': 121, 'first_round': '2026-07-28 00:13:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 12:42:00+00:00'}\ndev1/lead:0.5/crypto-24h {'reward_rank': 97, 'final_rank': 179, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.1487657406576099, 'reward_rounds': 87, 'first_round': '2026-07-28 00:13:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 13:00:00+00:00'}\ndev2/combined_exact:0.5:0.5/com-equ-24h {'reward_rank': 229, 'final_rank': 212, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.0012534078113477618, 'reward_rounds': 123, 'first_round': '2026-08-08 00:03:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-17 12:53:00+00:00'}\ndev2/combined_exact:0.5:0.5/crypto-24h {'reward_rank': 163, 'final_rank': 171, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.09609723754849869, 'reward_rounds': 85, 'first_round': '2026-08-08 00:23:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-17 12:55:00+00:00'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
