{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_260","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 28 — empirical clock resolution and shrinkage (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the current hourly clock and three-bin smoothing may blur repeatable volatility bursts. Its 25% profile floor and 25% shrinkage also enforce substantial dispersion in empirically quiet periods. These are modeling choices, not venue constraints.\n+- Change: against the lead-shaped incumbent, change one feature at a time: 30-minute versus hourly bins, 15-minute versus hourly bins, full versus 0.75 profile strength, or a 0.05 versus 0.25 positive profile floor. Keep the same within-day normalization, smoothing kernel, maximum profile value and seven-day context. Every bin remains strictly positive; no trading sessions, closures or external calendars are introduced.\n+- Result: pending both development windows. A score-only field diagnostic shows the largest weighted daily gaps are AAPLX, TSLAX, GOOGLX and NVDAX, not SP500 despite its higher coefficient. This diagnostic compares public aggregate score levels, never miners' served paths.\n+- Verdict: require consistent official CRPS and reward gains before combining with the temporal candidate.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n+\n+### Iteration 27 result\n+\n+Forecast-error mixtures fail the consistency gate at 1000 paths. Half conditional replacement gives COM_EQU CRPS ratios 0.99987/1.00065, hourly 1.00007/1.00038, daily crypto 1.00015/1.00099. Full replacement regresses further, and conditioning on the recent volatility trend barely differs from pooling. Discard these mixtures. The simpler Student mixture remains better calibrated than this empirical future-volatility uncertainty proxy.\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/clock_profile.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Strictly positive empirical variance clocks at different resolutions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+\n+def estimate_profile(context, timestamp, bins, floor):\n+    close = pd.to_numeric(context.close,errors='coerce')\n+    close = close.loc[(close.index>timestamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7)) & (close.index<=timestamp)]\n+    close = close.loc[np.isfinite(close)&(close>0)].sort_index()\n+    close = close.loc[~close.index.duplicated(keep='last')]\n+    if len(close)<2:\n+        return np.ones(bins)\n+    gaps = np.diff(close.index.as_unit('ns').asi8)/60e9\n+    absolute = np.abs(np.diff(np.log(close.to_numpy())))/np.sqrt(gaps)\n+    minute = close.index[1:].hour*60+close.index[1:].minute\n+    clock = pd.DataFrame({'absolute':absolute,'bin':minute*bins//1440,'day':close.index[1:].date})\n+    daily_mean = clock.groupby('day').absolute.transform('mean').clip(lower=1e-9)\n+    clock['relative'] = clock.absolute/daily_mean\n+    profile = clock.groupby('bin').relative.mean().reindex(range(bins),fill_value=1).to_numpy()\n+    profile = .25*np.roll(profile,1)+.5*profile+.25*np.roll(profile,-1)\n+    profile = np.clip(profile,floor,3)\n+    return profile/profile.mean()\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0] in ['location','periodic','uncertainty'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0] in ['combined','combined_exact'] else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n+    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0] in ['location','periodic','uncertainty','clock'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0] in ['combined','combined_exact'] else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n@@\n     uncertainty_parameters=parts[1:] if parts[0]=='uncertainty' else None\n+    clock_parameters=parts[1:] if parts[0]=='clock' else None\n@@\n     if cycle_strength and length > 3600:\n         future_times = pd.Timestamp(start_time) + pd.to_timedelta(np.arange(1,steps+1)*increment,unit='s')\n         profile = feature['cycle']\n+        clock_indices = future_times.hour\n+        if clock_parameters:\n+            from clock_profile import estimate_profile\n+\n+            bins,cycle_strength,floor = int(clock_parameters[0]),float(clock_parameters[1]),float(clock_parameters[2])\n+            profiles = feature.setdefault('clock_profiles',{})\n+            if (bins,floor) not in profiles:\n+                profiles[(bins,floor)] = estimate_profile(feature['context'],start_time,bins,floor)\n+            profile = profiles[(bins,floor)]\n+            clock_indices = (future_times.hour*60+future_times.minute)*bins//1440\n@@\n-        sigma *= 1 + cycle_strength*(profile[future_times.hour]-1)\n+        sigma *= 1 + cycle_strength*(profile[clock_indices]-1)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run agent/research.py --name clock_resolution_screen --variants lead:0.5,clock:48:0.75:0.25,clock:96:0.75:0.25,clock:24:1:0.25,clock:24:0.75:0.05 --format low --workers 4 > agent/clock_resolution_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
