{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_279","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat agent/BUDGET.md; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 31 — context-only adaptive calibration (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: a fixed pooled model can retain a slow-moving calibration bias on newer venues. Recently completed volatility forecasts inside the supplied seven-day context may identify that bias without retraining or external data.\n+- Change: reconstruct nine completed static-neural volatility forecasts using only observations available at each historical anchor, compare their predicted scales with subsequently observed absolute-return scales, and shrink the ratio of means by strengths 0.25/0.5. Hourly anchors cover the past nine completed hours; daily anchors span the past three days with six-hour spacing. Skip anchors preceding weight availability and require at least three usable forecasts. Cap the unshrunk ratio to [0.5,2].\n+- Result: pending official development CRPS against the lead-shaped incumbent. Overlapping daily labels are not treated as independent observations. Historical subcontexts are necessarily shorter than seven days and this approximation must be reported.\n+- Verdict: retain only if adaptation improves both regimes without destabilizing other competitions; otherwise prefer the fixed forecaster.\n+- Lesson: pending. Every calibration target ends by the actual prediction time, and no past served miner paths are used.\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/adaptive.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Causal calibration from completed, context-local volatility forecasts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+from modeling import WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM, _features, _learned_multiplier\n+\n+\n+def adaptive_ratio(context, timestamp, asset, length):\n+    timestamp = pd.Timestamp(timestamp)\n+    close = pd.to_numeric(context.close,errors='coerce')\n+    close = close.loc[(close.index>timestamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7)) & (close.index<=timestamp)]\n+    close = close.loc[np.isfinite(close)&(close>0)].sort_index()\n+    close = close.loc[~close.index.duplicated(keep='last')]\n+    if len(close)<50:\n+        return 1.\n+    gaps = np.diff(close.index.as_unit('ns').asi8)/60e9\n+    absolute = pd.Series(np.abs(np.diff(np.log(close.to_numpy())))/np.sqrt(gaps),index=close.index[1:])\n+    hourly = length<=3600\n+    horizon,spacing = (60,60) if hourly else (1440,360)\n+    actual,predicted = [],[]\n+    for offset in range(9):\n+        anchor = timestamp.floor('min')-pd.Timedelta(minutes=horizon+offset*spacing)\n+        if anchor<WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM:\n+            continue\n+        historical = close.loc[close.index<=anchor]\n+        realized = absolute.loc[(absolute.index>anchor)&(absolute.index<=anchor+pd.Timedelta(minutes=horizon))]\n+        if len(historical)<50 or len(realized)<max(10,horizon//10):\n+            continue\n+        scales,squares = _features(historical,anchor)\n+        forecast = scales[60 if hourly else 360]*_learned_multiplier(scales,squares,asset,hourly)\n+        actual.append(float(realized.mean()*np.sqrt(np.pi/2)))\n+        predicted.append(forecast)\n+    if len(actual)<3 or sum(predicted)<=0:\n+        return 1.\n+    return float(np.clip(sum(actual)/sum(predicted),.5,2.))\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0] in ['location','periodic','uncertainty','clock','sharp'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0] in ['combined','combined_exact'] else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n+    lead_strength=.5 if parts[0] in ['location','periodic','uncertainty','clock','sharp','adaptive'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0] in ['combined','combined_exact'] else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='lead' else None\n@@\n     joint_normalize=bool(int(parts[4])) if parts[0]=='sharp' else False\n+    adaptive_strength=float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='adaptive' else None\n@@\n         learned_scale=incumbent\n+        if adaptive_strength is not None:\n+            from adaptive import adaptive_ratio\n+\n+            corrections = feature.setdefault('adaptive',{})\n+            if length not in corrections:\n+                corrections[length] = adaptive_ratio(feature['context'],start_time,asset,length)\n+            learned_scale *= corrections[length]**adaptive_strength\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nwhile pgrep -f '\"'^/workspace/.venv/bin/python3 agent/fit_shape_score.py --fine '\"' >/dev/null; do sleep 5; done\nuv run agent/research.py --name adaptive_screen --variants lead:0.5,adaptive:0.25,adaptive:0.5 --workers 4 > agent/adaptive_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
