{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_355","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -n 20 agent/modeling.py; sed -n '1,12p' agent/report.md; cat agent/CHAMPION 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_355","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -n 20 agent/modeling.py; sed -n '1,12p' agent/report.md; cat agent/CHAMPION 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    steps = time_length // time_increment\n    if not hourly:\n        bins = (48 if asset in ASSETS[:5] else 96) if timestamp>=WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM else 24\n        cycle_strength = 1.0 if asset not in ASSETS[:5] and timestamp>=WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM else CYCLE_STRENGTH\n        profile = _volatility_profile(closes,bins)\n        future_times = timestamp + pd.to_timedelta(np.arange(1,steps+1)*time_increment,unit='s')\n        clock_indices = (future_times.hour*60+future_times.minute)*bins//1440\n        sigma *= 1 + cycle_strength*(profile[clock_indices]-1)\n        if timestamp >= WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM:\n            sigma *= _lead_profile(absolute,root_square,asset,steps,time_increment)\n    if timestamp >= WEIGHTS_AVAILABLE_FROM:\n        shocks = _sobol_shocks(num_simulations,steps,seed)\n    else:\n        shocks = rng.standard_normal(((num_simulations + 1) // 2, steps))\n        shocks = np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:num_simulations]\n        shocks *= np.sqrt(3 / rng.chisquare(5, size=(num_simulations, 1)))\n    log_paths = np.concatenate([np.zeros((num_simulations, 1)), np.cumsum(shocks * sigma, axis=1)], axis=1)\n    paths = last * np.exp(np.clip(log_paths, -40, 40))\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\n# Better volatility forecasts are not the same as better miner rewards\n\n**Status: interim research report. The campaign is active; no champion has been nominated.**\n\n## Context\n\nSynth SN50 asks a miner for a fan of future prices, not a single price target. This campaign covers all three competitions: five crypto assets at one-minute resolution for one hour, the same assets at five-minute resolution for one day, and eight live commodity/equity assets at five-minute resolution for one day. SPYX is retired and is not modeled or evaluated.\n\nEvery served prompt must contain the requested number of paths—1000 in the validator—and include the observed starting price. The daily and hourly shapes are therefore 1000 by 289 and 1000 by 61. Prices come only from the frozen snapshot, whose research cutoff is August 29, 2026. Nothing from the subsequent evaluation period is used.\n\nThe distinction between CRPS and emissions matters. The validator converts per-prompt CRPS into relative prompt scores, applies asset coefficients, smooths scores, and uses a softmax. An arithmetic average of CRPS across assets is not the campaign objective. The campaign's Score is 100 times the mean of the three capped reward ratios to each competition's best field miner.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_356","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/modeling.py\n@@\n-def simulate(\n+def _quote_tick(closes, last):\n+    digits = min(8,max(0,12-int(np.floor(np.log10(last)))))\n+    factor = 10.**digits\n+    if len(closes)<2 or closes.max()*factor>=np.iinfo(np.int64).max/4:\n+        return 0.\n+    integer_prices = np.rint(closes.to_numpy()*factor).astype(np.int64)\n+    return float(np.gcd.reduce(np.abs(np.diff(integer_prices)))/factor)\n+\n+\n+def simulate(\n@@\n     paths = last * np.exp(np.clip(log_paths, -40, 40))\n+    if hourly:\n+        tick = _quote_tick(closes,last)\n+        if 0<tick<last*.01:\n+            paths = np.maximum(tick,last+np.rint((paths-last)/tick)*tick)\n+            paths[:,0] = last\n     return (start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 32 full reward confirmation and promotion\n+\n+At every reward round and 1000 paths, GCD lattice projection raises hourly reward/best-field ratios from 0.869436/0.872234 to **0.950966/0.966341**. Cumulative ranks are 25/9 out of 257; final-round ranks are 55/1. Promote hourly projection only, while daily projection remains under confirmation. This is a roughly 0.05–0.09% asset-mean CRPS improvement with a much larger emissions effect, not evidence that CRPS and rewards are interchangeable.\n+\n+### Iteration 36 result\n+\n+Frozen Chronos-Bolt forecasts were generated for all 25,965 exact-context training/diagnostic rows. The existing stack's mean chronological likelihood is 1.007904. Neither intercept-only calibration (best tested 1.008133) nor pretrained-feature calibration (best tested 1.008303) improves it. Both selectors correctly retain zero coefficients. Reject before redundant field scoring. This bounded failure does not establish that all foundation models or fine-tuning would fail; it says this pretrained volatility representation adds no validated benefit with the tested small calibration.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,time\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom predict import load_context\nfrom modeling import simulate\nfrom research import features,generate_variant\nstamp=pd.Timestamp('2026-08-10 12:00',tz='UTC')\nfor asset in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE','SP500']:\n context=load_context(asset,stamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7),stamp)\n for length,increment in [(3600,60),(86400,300)]:\n  feature=features(context,stamp,increment)\n  variant='ticked:gcd' if length==3600 else 'stacked'\n  expected=generate_variant(feature,asset,stamp,increment,length,1000,variant)\n  started=time.perf_counter(); actual=np.asarray(simulate(asset,stamp,increment,length,1000,context)[2:]);latency=time.perf_counter()-started\n  np.testing.assert_allclose(actual,expected,rtol=1e-12,atol=0)\n  assert actual.shape==(1000,length//increment+1) and np.isfinite(actual).all() and (actual>0).all()\n  altered=context.copy();altered.iloc[::13]=np.nan\n  altered.loc[stamp+pd.Timedelta(minutes=1)]=1e20\n  forecast=np.asarray(simulate(asset,stamp,increment,length,17,altered)[2:])\n  assert forecast.shape==(17,length//increment+1) and np.isfinite(forecast).all() and (forecast>0).all()\n  np.testing.assert_array_equal(forecast,np.asarray(simulate(asset,stamp,increment,length,17,altered.loc[:stamp])[2:]))\n  print(asset,length,'match, contract',round(latency,4),flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
