{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_363","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/chronos_vol.py\n@@\n from functools import lru_cache\n+import os\n@@\n-    device = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n+    device = os.environ.get('CHRONOS_DEVICE', 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n*** Update File: agent/research.py\n@@\n-    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble']\n+    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree']\n+    tree_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stacktree' else None\n@@\n             learned_scale *= np.exp(temporal_strength*residual[0 if length==3600 else 1])\n+            if tree_strength is not None:\n+                from chronos_vol import forecast_features\n+                from tree_vol import tree_design, tree_residual\n+\n+                if 'chronos' not in feature:\n+                    feature['chronos'] = forecast_features(feature['temporal'][None])\n+                baseline_logs = np.log([learned_multiplier(feature,asset,3600,'neural')**.5,\n+                                        learned_multiplier(feature,asset,86400,'neural')])+residual\n+                design = tree_design(feature_vector(feature,asset)[None],feature['temporal'][None],\n+                                     [start_time],baseline_logs[None],feature['chronos'])['pretrained'][0]\n+                learned_scale *= np.exp(tree_strength*tree_residual(design)[0 if length==3600 else 1])\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 37 pre-field selection\n+\n+Shallow trees improve the chronological likelihood from 1.007904 to 1.006335 with static inputs, 1.004610 with temporal summaries/harmonics, and 1.004544 after adding pretrained summaries. The preregistered selector chooses the pretrained-feature model at 200 stages. Most of the improvement clearly comes from the non-pretrained temporal/clock summaries; the marginal pretrained gain is only 0.000066. The selected model now proceeds to half/full-strength official CRPS, without field-based tree hyperparameter selection.\n+\n+### Hourly projection serving audit correction\n+\n+The first ad-hoc comparison accidentally supplied an inclusive seven-day-left-endpoint frame to the research feature helper, whereas production and all field evaluations use a strict left boundary. The extra old observation changes long-memory neural features and breaks exact path equality. Correct the audit frame, not the already-correct field results or serving filter. This is distinct from the earlier temporal-cache boundary mismatch.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nCHRONOS_DEVICE=cpu HF_HOME=/workspace/.hf_cache HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 uv run agent/research.py --name tree_screen --variants stacked,stacktree:0.5,stacktree:1 --paths 1000 --workers 4 > agent/tree_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_364","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys,inspect\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nimport numpy as np\nfrom tree_vol import tree_weights,tree_residual\nfrom sklearn.ensemble._hist_gradient_boosting.predictor import TreePredictor\nprint(inspect.signature(TreePredictor.predict))\nweights=tree_weights();rng=np.random.default_rng(95);designs=rng.normal(size=(20,78))\nexpected=np.tile(weights['base'],(len(designs),1))\nfor head in range(2):\n for stage in range(int(weights['stages'])):\n  tree=TreePredictor(weights[f'{head}_{stage}'],np.zeros((0,8),dtype=np.uint32),np.zeros((0,8),dtype=np.uint32))\n  expected[:,head]+=tree.predict(designs,np.zeros((0,8),dtype=np.uint32),np.zeros(designs.shape[1],dtype=np.uint32),1)\nactual=np.stack([tree_residual(design) for design in designs])\nnp.testing.assert_allclose(actual,np.clip(expected,-.5,.5),rtol=1e-12,atol=1e-12)\nprint('Tree export matches sklearn traversal',np.max(np.abs(actual-np.clip(expected,-.5,.5))))\nprint('scores',100*(.9509663640460118+.2182216376+.0140754543)/3,100*(.9663407087771281+.1269506538+.0093654148)/3)\nPY\ncat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -n 6 agent/tree_screen.log; tail -n 3 agent/daily_lattice_periodic_dense.log; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
